WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:36.604
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

3
00:00:39.473 --> 00:00:42.576
(WIND WHISTLING)

4
00:00:53.154 --> 00:00:54.622
(AIR WHOOSHES)

5
00:00:55.123 --> 00:00:57.258
Whoever gets
to the temple first wins!

6
00:00:57.391 --> 00:00:59.593
What? Aang. no fair!

7
00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.462
(BLOWS RASPBERRY. GIGGLES)

8
00:01:01.562 --> 00:01:02.663
AIRBENDER 1:
Let's get him!

9
00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:04.165
AIRBENDER 2:
Come on. hurry up!

10
00:01:04.298 --> 00:01:05.899
(ALL GIGGLING)

11
00:01:09.237 --> 00:01:10.438
(ROARS)

12
00:01:12.206 --> 00:01:13.841
Hi. Nima.
Good morning. Aang.

13
00:01:13.974 --> 00:01:15.376
Hey. Mip-Mip.
Oh. hello. Aang.

14
00:01:15.509 --> 00:01:16.510
(GASPS)

15
00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.152
GYATSO: Oh. perfect timing.
Huh?

16
00:01:24.718 --> 00:01:26.086
(CHUCKLES)
Mind giving me a lift?

17
00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:28.122
Gyatso. this isn't
the best time.

18
00:01:28.256 --> 00:01:29.923
I'm getting old. you know.
(AIRBENDERS LAUGHING)

19
00:01:30.057 --> 00:01:32.226
My body doesn't move
like it used to.

20
00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.428
I'm kind of
in the middle of something.

21
00:01:34.562 --> 00:01:35.896
You are so heavy!

22
00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:39.267
GYATSO: Heavy? Me?
I eat nothing but vegetables.

23
00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.202
AANG: Pie is not a vegetable.

24
00:01:41.335 --> 00:01:42.803
I'm gonna lose the race!

25
00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:45.072
GYATSO: Race? What race?

26
00:01:45.206 --> 00:01:46.340
We finally won!

27
00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:47.641
We won! We won!

28
00:01:47.808 --> 00:01:49.810
(ALL LAUGHING)
Yay. we did it!

29
00:01:53.647 --> 00:01:56.083
Aang. as an Airbender.

30
00:01:56.217 --> 00:01:59.119
it's important that you know
when to show restraint.

31
00:02:00.588 --> 00:02:02.823
Even if you have
the power to win.

32
00:02:03.224 --> 00:02:04.625
you are the Avatar.

33
00:02:04.792 --> 00:02:08.862
A lot of people
are going to rely on you.
(ECHOES)

34
00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:09.863
(GASPS)

35
00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.065
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

36
00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:15.135
(GASPS)

37
00:02:15.769 --> 00:02:16.937
(YELPS)

38
00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:18.472
(GASPS)
(PEOPLE CLAMORING. SCREAMING)

39
00:02:18.639 --> 00:02:20.641
(GASPS)
WOMAN: Where's the Avatar?

40
00:02:20.774 --> 00:02:22.443
MAN: He's gone! He ran away!

41
00:02:22.576 --> 00:02:24.011
What? I'm here!

42
00:02:24.778 --> 00:02:27.348
MAN: Where's the Avatar?
WOMAN: Avatar!

43
00:02:27.781 --> 00:02:30.117
Aang! Where are you?

44
00:02:30.251 --> 00:02:31.819
Gyatso! I'm here!

45
00:02:34.822 --> 00:02:37.258
I'm... I'm... here!

46
00:02:37.391 --> 00:02:39.527
I'm here! I'm here!

47
00:02:39.693 --> 00:02:41.028
Here!

48
00:02:41.629 --> 00:02:42.696
I'm here.

49
00:02:42.863 --> 00:02:44.765
(PANTS. SIGHS)

50
00:02:44.865 --> 00:02:46.834
(PURRS)

51
00:02:46.967 --> 00:02:48.369
Hey. Momo.

52
00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:50.271
Hi. Appa.

53
00:02:50.371 --> 00:02:52.005
Was I asleep for long?
(GRUNTS)

54
00:02:52.139 --> 00:02:53.907
Okay. okay.
I'm awake already.

55
00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:56.844
I know. I know.
We've got a job to finish.

56
00:02:57.345 --> 00:03:00.147
(SIGHS)
Let's continue our journey.

57
00:03:00.648 --> 00:03:01.715
Back to our old home.

58
00:03:01.882 --> 00:03:04.285
(HOPEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

59
00:03:30.511 --> 00:03:33.113
(THUNDER RUMBLES)

60
00:03:43.657 --> 00:03:45.626
(MOMO CHITTERS)

61
00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:51.532
AANG: This may not
have been our best trip.

62
00:03:51.665 --> 00:03:54.768
but any Airbender relic we find
makes it all worthwhile.

63
00:04:00.474 --> 00:04:02.943
This could be the oldest piece
in our collection.

64
00:04:08.749 --> 00:04:10.284
"Sonam."

65
00:04:15.789 --> 00:04:17.991
(PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING)

66
00:04:21.562 --> 00:04:22.630
(SIGHS)

67
00:04:22.796 --> 00:04:24.031
I miss you.

68
00:04:26.367 --> 00:04:29.069
(MUSIC TURNS TENSE)

69
00:04:30.304 --> 00:04:32.506
Momo. go outside with Appa.
(CHITTERS)

70
00:04:32.606 --> 00:04:34.141
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

71
00:04:34.308 --> 00:04:35.376
Now!

72
00:04:35.509 --> 00:04:37.945
(ALL GRUNTING)

73
00:04:39.647 --> 00:04:40.814
AANG: Whoa!

74
00:04:42.049 --> 00:04:43.317
(JIE GRUNTS)

75
00:04:44.452 --> 00:04:46.720
Who are you?
Why are you doing this?

76
00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:49.189
(ALL GRUNTING)

77
00:04:50.658 --> 00:04:53.361
Please stop.
I don't want to hurt you.

78
00:04:55.596 --> 00:04:56.730
(KALLIK GROANS)
(YUDDAH YELLS)

79
00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:58.399
HONG: Where is it?
Where is it?

80
00:04:58.532 --> 00:04:59.900
No. that's not it.
(ANTIQUES SMASHING)

81
00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:01.335
Hey. those are antiques.

82
00:05:03.637 --> 00:05:05.406
(GRUNTS)

83
00:05:07.608 --> 00:05:09.109
(SHOUTS)

84
00:05:12.913 --> 00:05:14.214
Enough!

85
00:05:17.351 --> 00:05:20.087
HONG: Wait! I found it!
(YELPS)

86
00:05:21.789 --> 00:05:23.757
Sonam? Why are they after you?

87
00:05:24.825 --> 00:05:26.193
(YUDDAH GRUNTS)

88
00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:36.336
(GRUNTS)

89
00:05:39.673 --> 00:05:40.874
(GASPS)

90
00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:43.577
Wait!

91
00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:49.282
No! That's a thousand years old!

92
00:05:51.051 --> 00:05:53.487
(KALLIK GRUNTS)

93
00:05:53.721 --> 00:05:54.822
Give it to me!

94
00:05:54.955 --> 00:05:56.724
Why don't we just talk?
Maybe I can help.

95
00:05:56.857 --> 00:05:58.926
We don't need your help. Avatar.

96
00:05:59.693 --> 00:06:02.463
We're done living in a world
where Benders have all the power

97
00:06:02.596 --> 00:06:04.532
and we have none.
Who are you?

98
00:06:04.665 --> 00:06:05.733
We're the Denied.

99
00:06:05.866 --> 00:06:07.000
The Denied?

100
00:06:07.134 --> 00:06:08.335
JIE: Just kill him already!

101
00:06:08.469 --> 00:06:10.404
YUDDAH: No! You'll bring
the whole place down!

102
00:06:11.605 --> 00:06:12.740
(KALLIK GASPS)

103
00:06:14.575 --> 00:06:15.843
(MUSIC SOFTENS)

104
00:06:16.009 --> 00:06:17.244
(GRUNTS)

105
00:06:24.051 --> 00:06:25.586
(YELPS)

106
00:06:25.719 --> 00:06:28.622
(TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES)

107
00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:30.758
(WHIMPERS)

108
00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:35.328
(PANTING)

109
00:06:36.063 --> 00:06:37.130
(GROANING)

110
00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:39.266
You... saved me.

111
00:06:41.268 --> 00:06:43.471
JIE: Kallik. grab the map.
Let's go!

112
00:06:47.407 --> 00:06:49.577
(GRUNTING)

113
00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:50.511
(GASPS)

114
00:06:50.611 --> 00:06:52.379
(WOOD CREAKS)

115
00:06:52.513 --> 00:06:53.614
(GASPS)

116
00:06:54.782 --> 00:06:56.484
(ALL WHIMPERING)

117
00:06:57.618 --> 00:06:58.519
HONG: Oh. no!

118
00:06:58.619 --> 00:07:00.120
(AANG PANTING)

119
00:07:01.221 --> 00:07:02.322
(GRUNTS)

120
00:07:06.594 --> 00:07:09.362
(GRUNTING)

121
00:07:11.465 --> 00:07:13.834
(WHIMPERING)

122
00:07:15.669 --> 00:07:18.005
(STRUCTURE RUMBLING)

123
00:07:20.273 --> 00:07:22.610
(EPIC MUSIC PLAYING)

124
00:07:34.221 --> 00:07:35.489
(GRUNTS)

125
00:07:49.402 --> 00:07:50.638
(GRUNTS)

126
00:07:52.673 --> 00:07:54.374
(APPA GRUNTS)

127
00:07:54.975 --> 00:07:57.144
(CHITTERING)
(PANTING) I'm fine.

128
00:07:57.277 --> 00:07:58.646
Momo. I'm fine.

129
00:07:58.779 --> 00:08:00.080
(GROANING)

130
00:08:01.615 --> 00:08:03.551
But we've got
to get to Republic City.

131
00:08:04.685 --> 00:08:06.587
Appa. yip-yip!

132
00:08:23.804 --> 00:08:24.838
KATARA: <i>Water.</i>

133
00:08:25.305 --> 00:08:27.908
<i>Her tribes gather strength
from the moon</i>

134
00:08:28.942 --> 00:08:31.044
<i>and flow with the tides.</i>

135
00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:33.513
TOPH: <i>Earth.</i>

136
00:08:34.114 --> 00:08:39.653
<i>A kingdom of unshakable will.
reliable and strong.</i>

137
00:08:39.853 --> 00:08:41.589
(ROCKS RUMBLE)

138
00:08:42.723 --> 00:08:43.757
ZUKO: <i>Fire.</i>

139
00:08:44.324 --> 00:08:47.260
<i>A nation capable
of great destruction.</i>

140
00:08:48.461 --> 00:08:51.699
<i>but also of great warmth.</i>

141
00:08:52.065 --> 00:08:53.233
(FIRE WHOOSHES)

142
00:08:54.067 --> 00:08:55.202
AANG: <i>Air.</i>

143
00:08:55.468 --> 00:08:58.238
<i>Peaceful nomads with
the power of a hurricane.</i>

144
00:08:58.505 --> 00:09:01.041
<i>but the spirit
of a gentle breeze.</i>

145
00:09:03.143 --> 00:09:05.846
<i>For generations. the Avatar.</i>

146
00:09:05.979 --> 00:09:08.716
<i>the one master
of all four elements.</i>

147
00:09:08.882 --> 00:09:11.118
<i>kept the nations in balance.</i>

148
00:09:12.485 --> 00:09:16.156
<i>But when that responsibility
fell to me as a child.</i>

149
00:09:16.289 --> 00:09:17.490
<i>I ran away.</i>

150
00:09:17.891 --> 00:09:19.960
<i>I was caught in a deadly storm.</i>

151
00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:23.563
<i>but my Avatar spirit
preserved me
in a sphere of energy</i>

152
00:09:23.697 --> 00:09:27.567
<i>where I stayed
for a hundred years.</i>

153
00:09:27.735 --> 00:09:28.936
<i>I woke to discover</i>

154
00:09:29.069 --> 00:09:31.538
<i>that the balance
preserved by the Avatar</i>

155
00:09:31.672 --> 00:09:34.574
<i>had been destroyed by war.</i>

156
00:09:34.708 --> 00:09:37.077
<i>The Air Nomads were gone.</i>

157
00:09:37.778 --> 00:09:39.412
<i>All but one.</i>

158
00:09:39.546 --> 00:09:40.413
<i>Me.</i>

159
00:09:41.014 --> 00:09:43.516
<i>I could no longer run
from my responsibility</i>

160
00:09:43.617 --> 00:09:45.052
<i>as the Avatar.</i>

161
00:09:45.819 --> 00:09:48.421
<i>I found allies
from every nation.</i>

162
00:09:48.856 --> 00:09:51.291
<i>Benders and Nonbenders.</i>

163
00:09:52.993 --> 00:09:54.928
<i>Katara taught me
how to waterbend.</i>

164
00:09:55.595 --> 00:09:58.598
<i>Toph trained me in the ways
of the Earthbenders.</i>

165
00:09:59.199 --> 00:10:03.704
<i>Zuko. once my worst enemy.
became my firebending teacher.</i>

166
00:10:04.471 --> 00:10:08.008
<i>Sokka showed me that bravery
is the most important part</i>

167
00:10:08.108 --> 00:10:10.210
<i>of being a leader.</i>

168
00:10:10.343 --> 00:10:12.345
<i>We became a family.</i>

169
00:10:13.246 --> 00:10:16.750
<i>And together. we ended
the Hundred Year War.</i>

170
00:10:17.785 --> 00:10:22.489
<i>Then. we began the hard work
of rebuilding the world.</i>

171
00:10:22.622 --> 00:10:25.292
(EPIC MUSIC PLAYING)

172
00:10:34.101 --> 00:10:37.104
KATARA: <i>For so long.
the nation stood apart.</i>

173
00:10:37.237 --> 00:10:38.138
<i>alone.</i>

174
00:10:38.538 --> 00:10:40.040
<i>and we all suffered
as a result.</i>

175
00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:43.043
<i>But here.
on this ancient site.</i>

176
00:10:43.143 --> 00:10:45.779
<i>we created a place
where all people are welcome.</i>

177
00:10:46.313 --> 00:10:48.415
<i>Bender and Nonbender alike.</i>

178
00:10:48.515 --> 00:10:52.319
<i>working together in peace
to build the future.</i>

179
00:10:52.452 --> 00:10:54.788
<i>Though there are still
those who would seek</i>

180
00:10:54.922 --> 00:10:57.791
to divide us.
we remain united.

181
00:10:58.425 --> 00:10:59.893
As a council representative.

182
00:10:59.993 --> 00:11:02.162
I am honored
to be here today

183
00:11:02.295 --> 00:11:05.198
celebrating the anniversary
of Republic City

184
00:11:05.365 --> 00:11:07.534
and the opening
of Unity Tower.

185
00:11:07.701 --> 00:11:10.037
a symbol for all people.

186
00:11:14.541 --> 00:11:16.309
(CROWD CHEERING)

187
00:11:16.443 --> 00:11:17.544
Look!

188
00:11:17.711 --> 00:11:18.812
Yeah!

189
00:11:18.946 --> 00:11:20.714
It's the Avatar!

190
00:11:22.149 --> 00:11:23.683
(CHUCKLES)

191
00:11:23.851 --> 00:11:26.353
Whoo!
Whoo!

192
00:11:27.054 --> 00:11:28.688
(BOTH GROANING)

193
00:11:28.822 --> 00:11:29.923
(SIGHS)

194
00:11:32.025 --> 00:11:33.193
Momo!

195
00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:35.495
(CHITTERING)
(GIGGLES)

196
00:11:35.628 --> 00:11:37.197
(CHUCKLES) Appa!

197
00:11:37.330 --> 00:11:39.299
I missed you too.
old friend.

198
00:11:41.401 --> 00:11:42.535
Aang!

199
00:11:42.702 --> 00:11:43.570
Katara!

200
00:11:43.737 --> 00:11:44.738
KATARA: Mm!

201
00:11:46.139 --> 00:11:47.707
(KISSES)
(GROANS)

202
00:11:48.876 --> 00:11:50.210
You're hurt.

203
00:11:54.081 --> 00:11:56.917
(PEACEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

204
00:11:57.818 --> 00:11:59.319
KATARA: Take a deep breath.

205
00:11:59.419 --> 00:12:01.421
(AANG INHALES)

206
00:12:01.588 --> 00:12:03.924
KATARA: And... exhale.

207
00:12:04.057 --> 00:12:05.058
(AANG EXHALES)

208
00:12:05.192 --> 00:12:07.194
I've heard the Denied
are growing in numbers.

209
00:12:07.327 --> 00:12:09.396
but they've never
done anything like this.

210
00:12:09.529 --> 00:12:10.764
Attacking the Avatar?

211
00:12:10.931 --> 00:12:12.232
Yeah.

212
00:12:12.365 --> 00:12:14.101
They were incredible fighters.

213
00:12:14.601 --> 00:12:16.403
Even without bending.

214
00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:18.005
(BACK CRACKS)
(SHOUTS)

215
00:12:18.105 --> 00:12:20.540
Oops. Breathe through it.
Ow! (GROANS)

216
00:12:20.673 --> 00:12:22.609
Be honest.
You're enjoying this.

217
00:12:22.742 --> 00:12:24.711
Aang. this is serious.

218
00:12:24.845 --> 00:12:26.679
Whatever this map
they took was.

219
00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:29.416
if they were willing
to kill the Avatar to get it.

220
00:12:29.549 --> 00:12:31.451
what else
are they willing to do?

221
00:12:31.952 --> 00:12:33.854
I don't know.

222
00:12:33.987 --> 00:12:35.522
I'm worried about you.

223
00:12:36.189 --> 00:12:37.690
You're spending more
and more time

224
00:12:37.791 --> 00:12:39.793
at the Air Temple. alone.

225
00:12:41.094 --> 00:12:43.831
It's how I hold on to my past.

226
00:12:45.866 --> 00:12:48.268
I know how hard
this is for you.

227
00:12:49.602 --> 00:12:50.838
(SIGHS)

228
00:12:52.372 --> 00:12:53.974
When I was attacked.

229
00:12:54.607 --> 00:12:57.010
all I could think about
was that...

230
00:12:57.744 --> 00:12:59.279
this could be it.

231
00:13:00.647 --> 00:13:03.283
I'm the last Airbender.

232
00:13:04.551 --> 00:13:08.621
If I die.
my culture dies with me.

233
00:13:11.291 --> 00:13:15.228
You may be the last Airbender.
but you're not alone.

234
00:13:15.929 --> 00:13:19.967
Aang. none of this
would exist without you.

235
00:13:21.168 --> 00:13:23.570
You made the city possible
with your heart

236
00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:25.038
and your mind.

237
00:13:26.606 --> 00:13:27.941
Because of you...

238
00:13:28.441 --> 00:13:30.477
all of the nations
live here...

239
00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:31.845
together.

240
00:13:33.813 --> 00:13:35.482
All except mine.

241
00:13:45.492 --> 00:13:46.693
I know...

242
00:13:47.027 --> 00:13:49.829
but the people here
still need your protection.

243
00:13:50.463 --> 00:13:52.900
You're an Airbender...

244
00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:55.002
but you're also the Avatar.

245
00:13:57.204 --> 00:13:58.438
You're right.

246
00:13:59.506 --> 00:14:03.376
Whoever this Sonam person is.
I need to find out more.

247
00:14:15.522 --> 00:14:18.358
(VOICES WHISPERING)

248
00:14:29.169 --> 00:14:30.270
Aang.

249
00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:31.538
AANG: Avatar Roku.

250
00:14:31.704 --> 00:14:34.041
ROKU: It is good
to see you again.

251
00:14:34.207 --> 00:14:35.542
How can I help you?

252
00:14:35.708 --> 00:14:37.677
In your lifetime.
did you ever hear

253
00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:40.080
of an ancient Airbender
named Sonam?

254
00:14:40.213 --> 00:14:41.414
I have not.

255
00:14:41.548 --> 00:14:44.684
but you have many
past lives to call upon.

256
00:14:44.817 --> 00:14:47.487
Perhaps one further back
in the Avatar cycle

257
00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:49.256
can help you.

258
00:14:49.689 --> 00:14:51.058
Thank you. Avatar Roku.

259
00:14:51.224 --> 00:14:53.260
(VOICES WHISPERING)

260
00:14:53.393 --> 00:14:55.162
I'm sorry.
I've never heard of Sonam.

261
00:14:55.295 --> 00:14:56.964
I'm unfamiliar.
PAST AVATAR: Perhaps earlier.

262
00:14:57.064 --> 00:14:58.398
You must go further back.

263
00:14:58.898 --> 00:15:00.533
PAST AVATARS. OVERLAPPING:
You must go further back.
Not here.

264
00:15:00.667 --> 00:15:02.402
...in the Avatar Cycle.

265
00:15:03.903 --> 00:15:05.705
(VOICES FADE)

266
00:15:09.076 --> 00:15:10.944
AANG: Um. hello?

267
00:15:11.945 --> 00:15:13.480
Is there anyone here?

268
00:15:14.681 --> 00:15:15.983
Hello?

269
00:15:16.083 --> 00:15:17.117
(GRUNTS)

270
00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:20.720
XIAN: (IN BOOMING VOICE)
Who calls upon Avatar Xian's

271
00:15:20.853 --> 00:15:23.156
vast wealth of knowledge?

272
00:15:24.557 --> 00:15:26.793
(XIAN COUGHS. CLEARS THROAT)

273
00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:28.128
(IN NORMAL VOICE)
Oh. hello.

274
00:15:28.428 --> 00:15:31.965
You look like an Avatar
from a time
quite distant from mine.

275
00:15:32.099 --> 00:15:34.934
Please. please.
tell me about your era.

276
00:15:35.068 --> 00:15:36.703
What are people wearing?

277
00:15:36.803 --> 00:15:38.405
Are sandals still a thing?

278
00:15:38.538 --> 00:15:39.772
Uh. yes.

279
00:15:39.906 --> 00:15:41.208
(SCOFFS) Why?

280
00:15:41.308 --> 00:15:43.610
Why. after so many years.

281
00:15:43.743 --> 00:15:47.647
open toes. seeing someone
else's crusty cuticles?

282
00:15:47.947 --> 00:15:49.316
Disgusting!

283
00:15:49.482 --> 00:15:50.450
Right.

284
00:15:50.683 --> 00:15:52.652
Anyway. I have come
for your guidance.

285
00:15:52.785 --> 00:15:54.221
You see. I was attacked.

286
00:15:54.321 --> 00:15:56.323
It was not me. okay?
Wasn't me.

287
00:15:56.456 --> 00:15:57.490
I know that.

288
00:15:57.624 --> 00:15:58.925
I think it might have
something to do

289
00:15:59.059 --> 00:16:00.827
with an Airbender named Sonam.

290
00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:02.829
Hmm. Sonam.

291
00:16:02.962 --> 00:16:04.597
It sounds familiar.

292
00:16:04.731 --> 00:16:07.234
Sonam.
Where have I heard
that name before?

293
00:16:07.334 --> 00:16:08.335
(GASPS) Ah-ha!

294
00:16:08.501 --> 00:16:10.103
Sonam was the youngest daughter
of the owner

295
00:16:10.237 --> 00:16:12.439
of the possum-chicken shop
at the corner marketplace.

296
00:16:12.572 --> 00:16:15.308
Wait. that was my ex.
So Nyung.

297
00:16:15.475 --> 00:16:18.611
If only she didn't have
those humongous toenails.

298
00:16:18.745 --> 00:16:20.347
(GROANS) Disgusting.

299
00:16:20.513 --> 00:16:21.581
This is going nowhere.

300
00:16:21.714 --> 00:16:23.316
Sonam... So-nahm...
Sonum?

301
00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:25.852
(SIGHS) Well.
thank you for your time.

302
00:16:26.019 --> 00:16:27.920
I must continue my search.

303
00:16:28.055 --> 00:16:29.922
Oh. Sonam!

304
00:16:30.057 --> 00:16:34.127
You're asking about the legend
of the lost Avatar.

305
00:16:34.494 --> 00:16:36.129
Sonam was an Avatar?

306
00:16:36.263 --> 00:16:37.830
Indeed she was!

307
00:16:37.964 --> 00:16:39.632
She was the Avatar

308
00:16:39.766 --> 00:16:42.469
in the golden age
of Airbenders.

309
00:16:42.602 --> 00:16:45.305
Legend said she had
a staff that could channel

310
00:16:45.438 --> 00:16:48.241
the vast energy
of the Spirit World.

311
00:16:48.341 --> 00:16:51.644
granting its keeper
unlimited power.

312
00:16:51.778 --> 00:16:54.081
Is... Is that even possible?

313
00:16:55.014 --> 00:16:57.050
Eh. we'll never know for sure.

314
00:16:57.184 --> 00:16:59.686
Many Avatars have tried
to communicate with her.

315
00:16:59.819 --> 00:17:00.853
but they couldn't.

316
00:17:00.987 --> 00:17:02.555
She disappeared
so completely

317
00:17:02.689 --> 00:17:05.558
that it was as if
she never existed.

318
00:17:05.725 --> 00:17:07.860
And perhaps
it's better that way.

319
00:17:08.361 --> 00:17:10.697
Maybe such a staff
was too dangerous

320
00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:14.501
for anyone to possess.
even the Avatar.

321
00:17:14.634 --> 00:17:17.204
But... But that's exactly
why I need to find it.

322
00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:20.006
The people who attacked me
discovered a map.

323
00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:21.841
It must lead to the staff.

324
00:17:22.275 --> 00:17:24.211
Avatar Xian. please.

325
00:17:24.377 --> 00:17:26.579
you have to tell me
where it is.

326
00:17:28.848 --> 00:17:32.552
The legend says that Sonam
disappeared with her staff

327
00:17:32.719 --> 00:17:35.122
on the peak
of Mount Baihu.

328
00:17:37.557 --> 00:17:40.493
AANG: <i>"Katara. I'm sorry
to leave so suddenly.</i>

329
00:17:40.593 --> 00:17:42.729
<i>but I found out
what the Denied are after."</i>

330
00:17:43.496 --> 00:17:45.832
<i>"Sonam had a staff
of immense power.</i>

331
00:17:46.299 --> 00:17:47.434
<i>and in their hands.</i>

332
00:17:47.567 --> 00:17:49.736
<i>it could be
a devastating weapon."</i>

333
00:17:50.337 --> 00:17:51.804
<i>"They have a head start."</i>

334
00:17:51.904 --> 00:17:53.473
<i>"There's no time to waste."</i>

335
00:17:54.407 --> 00:17:57.510
<i>"You take Appa and Momo
and gather up
the rest of the team."</i>

336
00:17:57.610 --> 00:17:59.146
<i>"We're gonna need some help."</i>

337
00:18:05.718 --> 00:18:06.986
GRAND CHAMBERLAIN:
Next on the agenda.

338
00:18:07.086 --> 00:18:09.055
a Fire Nation naval vessel
came into conflict

339
00:18:09.189 --> 00:18:12.192
with an extremist group
of Nonbenders called the Denied.

340
00:18:12.292 --> 00:18:15.362
They've been
robbing ancient sites...
Your Majesty! Your Majesty!

341
00:18:15.495 --> 00:18:18.131
An urgent message has arrived
from Republic City.

342
00:18:18.265 --> 00:18:19.399
How impudent.

343
00:18:19.532 --> 00:18:21.100
Can't you see
Fire Lord Zuko is...

344
00:18:21.234 --> 00:18:22.435
ZUKO: Chamberlain.

345
00:18:23.303 --> 00:18:25.037
There's only one person
who can send a message

346
00:18:25.138 --> 00:18:27.407
urgent enough to interrupt
the Fire Lord's counsel.

347
00:18:27.774 --> 00:18:29.676
Is it from the Avatar?
MESSENGER: Yes. my lord.

348
00:18:29.776 --> 00:18:32.579
ZUKO: Read it to me.
Yes. my lord.

349
00:18:32.712 --> 00:18:34.614
(CLEARS THROAT)

350
00:18:34.747 --> 00:18:36.115
Um... (CLEARS THROAT)

351
00:18:36.283 --> 00:18:37.384
What are you doing?

352
00:18:37.484 --> 00:18:38.585
Read it quickly.

353
00:18:38.718 --> 00:18:41.087
Uh... Yeah. yeah.
Yes. Grand Chamberlain.

354
00:18:41.221 --> 00:18:42.355
(CLEARS THROAT)

355
00:18:42.455 --> 00:18:45.325
"Flameo Hotman.
how's ruling the Fire Nation?"

356
00:18:45.492 --> 00:18:49.162
"I hope the boring Chamberlain
you mention in your letters

357
00:18:49.296 --> 00:18:51.798
isn't still annoying you."
(ALL GASP)

358
00:18:51.931 --> 00:18:54.967
"Anyhoo. to cut to the chase.
I need your help."
(SIGHS)

359
00:18:55.134 --> 00:18:57.136
MESSENGER: "Can you please
come immediately?"

360
00:18:57.270 --> 00:19:01.140
"Oh. and don't forget to bring
some firecracker buns."

361
00:19:01.274 --> 00:19:02.542
(SIGHS)

362
00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:06.179
SOKKA: <i>Allow me
to present Sokka-Cycle.</i>

363
00:19:06.313 --> 00:19:07.680
Flames launch you into the sky

364
00:19:07.814 --> 00:19:10.350
where you can drop
water bombs on your enemies.

365
00:19:10.517 --> 00:19:13.186
then skis pop out
to help you stick the landing.

366
00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:14.821
(CHUCKLES)
Pretty great. right?

367
00:19:14.954 --> 00:19:16.122
Eh. boring.

368
00:19:16.489 --> 00:19:18.458
Why would you need a sled
when you can just waterbend?

369
00:19:18.591 --> 00:19:20.126
Ooh. ooh. ooh.
Like me. like me!

370
00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:21.160
Whee!

371
00:19:21.328 --> 00:19:22.495
Keep in mind.
there are still

372
00:19:22.629 --> 00:19:24.431
plenty of folks like me
who can't bend.

373
00:19:24.564 --> 00:19:27.133
Why would Avatar Aang
partner with a Nonbender?

374
00:19:27.267 --> 00:19:29.869
(GROANS) Why?
I'll tell you why.

375
00:19:30.002 --> 00:19:31.438
<i>I saved him from the iceberg.</i>

376
00:19:31.538 --> 00:19:32.905
<i>My boomerang flew by his side</i>

377
00:19:33.005 --> 00:19:35.375
<i>while I parried away enemies
with my trusty blade.</i>

378
00:19:35.542 --> 00:19:38.845
<i>I even took down the whole
Fire Nation airship armada.</i>

379
00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:42.081
<i>And on top of all that.</i>

380
00:19:42.181 --> 00:19:44.083
<i>I was more popular than him.</i>

381
00:19:45.218 --> 00:19:46.686
You're such a liar. Sokka.

382
00:19:46.853 --> 00:19:49.789
(CHIRPING)

383
00:19:49.889 --> 00:19:51.057
SOKKA:
It's from the Avatar.

384
00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:52.892
Really?
That's so cool!
Wow.

385
00:19:53.025 --> 00:19:54.861
Oh. so now
you think I'm cool?

386
00:19:54.994 --> 00:19:55.895
(CHILDREN GIGGLING)

387
00:19:56.062 --> 00:19:58.030
TOPH: <i>All right. Metalbenders.</i>

388
00:19:58.197 --> 00:20:00.267
Let's see if
any of you tenderfoots

389
00:20:00.367 --> 00:20:02.034
can at least make me
use my hands.

390
00:20:02.168 --> 00:20:03.570
(GRUNTS)

391
00:20:03.703 --> 00:20:05.104
(METAL WHIRRING)

392
00:20:09.208 --> 00:20:11.244
(UPBEAT TRIBAL MUSIC PLAYING)

393
00:20:11.411 --> 00:20:13.246
(ALL GRUNTING)

394
00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:22.021
(SIGHS)

395
00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:24.524
(GROANS)

396
00:20:24.657 --> 00:20:25.892
(GRUNTS)

397
00:20:28.761 --> 00:20:31.764
(BOTH GRUNTING)
(METAL CLANGS)

398
00:20:35.201 --> 00:20:38.104
I'm still the greatest
Earthbender in the world!

399
00:20:38.271 --> 00:20:39.272
(BIRD SCREECHES)

400
00:20:39.606 --> 00:20:40.773
And I'm bored.

401
00:20:41.274 --> 00:20:43.743
Master Toph.
there's a bird on your head.

402
00:20:43.910 --> 00:20:46.279
And?
It looks like it has a message.

403
00:20:46.413 --> 00:20:47.246
TOPH: Read.

404
00:20:47.714 --> 00:20:50.450
Uh. it's from Avatar Aang.
He needs your help.

405
00:20:50.617 --> 00:20:52.018
It's the Denied?
The Denied?

406
00:20:52.118 --> 00:20:53.185
Where is he?

407
00:20:53.286 --> 00:20:54.787
Mount Baihu.

408
00:20:54.954 --> 00:20:58.090
(WIND WHISTLING)
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

409
00:21:18.277 --> 00:21:22.449
(AIR WHOOSHING)

410
00:21:23.115 --> 00:21:24.250
(GRUNTS)

411
00:21:24.384 --> 00:21:27.286
(PANTS)

412
00:21:28.421 --> 00:21:29.689
(GRUNTS)

413
00:21:30.189 --> 00:21:32.492
(WIND HOWLING)

414
00:21:45.805 --> 00:21:47.006
(GRUNTS)

415
00:21:47.940 --> 00:21:49.776
(YELPS)

416
00:21:51.811 --> 00:21:54.547
(WHIMPERING)

417
00:21:57.183 --> 00:21:58.851
No. no. no!

418
00:21:59.018 --> 00:22:00.353
No!

419
00:22:01.120 --> 00:22:02.355
(GROANS)

420
00:22:03.923 --> 00:22:05.725
I love that hat.

421
00:22:12.298 --> 00:22:14.367
(PANTING)
(WIND HOWLING)

422
00:22:29.148 --> 00:22:32.385
(MUSIC TURNS SERENE)

423
00:22:35.021 --> 00:22:37.424
(PANTS)
(TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES)

424
00:22:40.026 --> 00:22:43.430
(MUSIC INTENSIFIES)

425
00:22:46.966 --> 00:22:48.435
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

426
00:22:49.168 --> 00:22:50.403
(GRUNTS)

427
00:22:53.372 --> 00:22:54.407
(GRUNTS)

428
00:22:54.541 --> 00:22:56.409
(PANTING)

429
00:22:57.076 --> 00:23:00.379
(MUSIC SOFTENS)

430
00:23:09.088 --> 00:23:13.426
(CURIOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

431
00:23:32.111 --> 00:23:35.682
(SNOW RUMBLING)

432
00:23:37.416 --> 00:23:40.487
(RUMBLING CONTINUES)

433
00:23:47.627 --> 00:23:49.962
(ETHEREAL MUSIC PLAYING)

434
00:23:50.129 --> 00:23:51.531
Sonam?

435
00:23:56.268 --> 00:23:58.004
Could that be you?

436
00:24:00.172 --> 00:24:01.340
(GRUNTS)

437
00:24:05.645 --> 00:24:07.480
(ICE RUMBLING AND CRACKLING)

438
00:24:10.950 --> 00:24:11.851
(GRUNTS)

439
00:24:12.018 --> 00:24:13.986
(CRACKLING)
(AIR HISSING)

440
00:24:24.597 --> 00:24:25.565
(SHOUTS)

441
00:24:32.972 --> 00:24:35.742
(WIND HOWLING)

442
00:24:38.144 --> 00:24:39.378
(GASPS)

443
00:24:49.188 --> 00:24:50.690
(EXHALES)

444
00:24:54.093 --> 00:24:55.427
(PANTING)

445
00:25:01.200 --> 00:25:02.401
Who are you?

446
00:25:02.569 --> 00:25:04.403
(CRACKLING)
Huh?

447
00:25:08.941 --> 00:25:11.243
(RUMBLING)

448
00:25:13.112 --> 00:25:15.247
(GRUNTING. PANTING)

449
00:25:15.414 --> 00:25:17.984
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

450
00:25:24.090 --> 00:25:26.993
(ICE GROANING)
(GRUNTS)

451
00:25:31.330 --> 00:25:34.033
(MUSIC INTENSIFIES)

452
00:25:50.516 --> 00:25:52.051
(PANTING)

453
00:25:53.119 --> 00:25:55.588
(WHIMPERING)

454
00:26:11.570 --> 00:26:12.672
(GASPS)

455
00:26:18.811 --> 00:26:20.346
(GASPS. GRUNTS)

456
00:26:21.013 --> 00:26:22.649
(PANTING)

457
00:26:27.119 --> 00:26:28.420
(GRUNTS)

458
00:26:40.099 --> 00:26:42.869
(WHIMPERING)

459
00:26:47.139 --> 00:26:48.641
(SHOUTS)

460
00:27:04.090 --> 00:27:05.658
(THUDS)
(MUSIC ENDS ABRUPTLY)

461
00:27:05.792 --> 00:27:08.027
(SCREAMS)

462
00:27:09.796 --> 00:27:12.198
(SOFT MUSIC PLAYING)

463
00:27:28.981 --> 00:27:32.318
(MUSIC TURNS DRAMATIC)

464
00:27:42.228 --> 00:27:44.396
(ROCK CRACKLING)

465
00:27:54.640 --> 00:27:55.942
Aang!

466
00:27:59.912 --> 00:28:01.247
(BOTH GRUNT)

467
00:28:06.252 --> 00:28:07.619
(APPA GROANS)

468
00:28:14.994 --> 00:28:17.396
(GROWLS)

469
00:28:17.529 --> 00:28:19.098
(MUSIC TURNS VICTORIOUS)

470
00:28:23.602 --> 00:28:26.272
Team Avatar to the rescue!

471
00:28:26.438 --> 00:28:27.506
(MUSIC SOFTENS)

472
00:28:27.606 --> 00:28:28.908
KATARA: Aang!

473
00:28:29.475 --> 00:28:30.509
You made it!

474
00:28:31.210 --> 00:28:33.279
You couldn't wait a day
before running off
to get yourself killed?

475
00:28:33.445 --> 00:28:36.015
I thought you were here
looking for a staff.

476
00:28:36.115 --> 00:28:37.416
Who's this guy?

477
00:28:38.250 --> 00:28:40.586
(SOFT HOPEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)
(MOMO CHITTERING)

478
00:28:40.719 --> 00:28:43.189
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

479
00:28:44.056 --> 00:28:45.792
An Airbender.

480
00:28:47.927 --> 00:28:49.261
(PANTS)

481
00:28:52.564 --> 00:28:53.833
(GROANS)

482
00:28:58.370 --> 00:29:01.974
(BIRDS CHIRPING)
(WATER RIPPLING)

483
00:29:06.445 --> 00:29:08.848
SOKKA: How did he hold up
an entire mountain?

484
00:29:08.948 --> 00:29:12.351
KATARA: His chi is strong.
like nothing I've ever felt.

485
00:29:13.619 --> 00:29:16.188
Hey. Avatar. you think
this guy beat your record

486
00:29:16.288 --> 00:29:18.357
for longest frozen Airbender?

487
00:29:18.457 --> 00:29:21.560
Yeah. How long do you think
he was in that ice?

488
00:29:21.693 --> 00:29:22.862
I don't know.

489
00:29:23.262 --> 00:29:25.731
His tattoos look... ancient.

490
00:29:26.198 --> 00:29:28.100
He's been in there a long time.

491
00:29:28.234 --> 00:29:29.735
He smells good for an old guy.

492
00:29:29.836 --> 00:29:30.669
Ew.
What?

493
00:29:31.070 --> 00:29:32.638
My senses tell me this guy
is pretty attractive.

494
00:29:32.805 --> 00:29:34.006
Toph!
Someone else confirm.

495
00:29:34.173 --> 00:29:35.942
This is serious.
What does attractive even mean?

496
00:29:36.075 --> 00:29:37.643
Just give me
a straight confirmation.

497
00:29:37.776 --> 00:29:38.845
Is he attractive?

498
00:29:39.278 --> 00:29:40.880
He's very attractive.
AANG AND KATARA: Huh?

499
00:29:41.680 --> 00:29:43.482
What? He is.

500
00:29:43.615 --> 00:29:44.951
It's all in the bone structure.

501
00:29:45.084 --> 00:29:46.618
MAN: No...
(BOTH GASP)

502
00:29:47.987 --> 00:29:49.421
No...

503
00:29:49.521 --> 00:29:50.389
No!

504
00:29:50.489 --> 00:29:52.124
Whoa. whoa. whoa. Hey.

505
00:29:52.258 --> 00:29:54.193
Easy. you're safe.

506
00:29:54.360 --> 00:29:55.828
(HEART BEATING)

507
00:29:56.495 --> 00:29:58.030
MAN: Earthbender!
AANG: No. no. no!

508
00:29:58.197 --> 00:30:00.166
We're all friends here.
It's okay.

509
00:30:00.632 --> 00:30:02.134
Someone woke up
on the wrong side

510
00:30:02.268 --> 00:30:03.435
of the mountain.

511
00:30:04.170 --> 00:30:05.237
Where is she?

512
00:30:05.337 --> 00:30:06.672
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

513
00:30:06.805 --> 00:30:08.607
Where is Avatar Sonam?

514
00:30:08.707 --> 00:30:10.209
You knew Sonam?

515
00:30:11.510 --> 00:30:12.845
Who are you?

516
00:30:13.345 --> 00:30:15.547
I don't know how to explain it.

517
00:30:15.714 --> 00:30:17.884
but you've been asleep
for a long time.

518
00:30:19.185 --> 00:30:20.819
I'm the Avatar now.

519
00:30:21.153 --> 00:30:22.154
I'm Aang.

520
00:30:23.022 --> 00:30:26.392
(PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING)
If you're the Avatar. then...

521
00:30:27.359 --> 00:30:28.560
Sonam...

522
00:30:30.863 --> 00:30:33.832
Well. Sonam might be long gone.

523
00:30:33.966 --> 00:30:36.969
but on the bright side.
you woke up at the perfect time.

524
00:30:37.103 --> 00:30:39.738
Everyone will be amazed
to see another Airbender.

525
00:30:39.872 --> 00:30:42.274
Aang's not the last one anymore.

526
00:30:43.575 --> 00:30:45.945
What do you mean. last?

527
00:30:46.045 --> 00:30:47.246
(GULPS)

528
00:30:49.982 --> 00:30:53.719
The Air Nomads.
they've been wiped out.

529
00:30:55.421 --> 00:30:56.722
There's only me.

530
00:30:58.524 --> 00:30:59.758
No.

531
00:31:00.392 --> 00:31:03.162
Sonam's staff.
do you have it?

532
00:31:03.729 --> 00:31:05.131
It's our only hope now.

533
00:31:05.864 --> 00:31:07.099
What do you mean?

534
00:31:07.266 --> 00:31:08.867
I thought it was a weapon.

535
00:31:09.936 --> 00:31:11.703
The staff is no weapon.

536
00:31:12.438 --> 00:31:13.805
It is a gift.

537
00:31:16.242 --> 00:31:18.710
<i>With it.
Sonam was able to channel</i>

538
00:31:18.844 --> 00:31:20.913
<i>the vast power
of the Spirit World.</i>

539
00:31:21.580 --> 00:31:25.117
<i>It was this power that
allowed Jharana to flourish.</i>

540
00:31:25.617 --> 00:31:29.922
<i>The greatest city in the world.
an Air Nomad utopia.</i>

541
00:31:30.089 --> 00:31:33.960
<i>where Sonam presided
over a golden age of balance</i>

542
00:31:34.126 --> 00:31:37.563
<i>and where I devoted my life
to serving her.</i>

543
00:31:38.097 --> 00:31:39.966
<i>In return. she raised me up</i>

544
00:31:40.132 --> 00:31:44.270
<i>and used her staff to give me.
a lowly Nonbender.</i>

545
00:31:44.403 --> 00:31:46.672
<i>the power to bend the air.</i>

546
00:31:47.706 --> 00:31:50.776
<i>I was the first.
but I would not be the last.</i>

547
00:31:51.610 --> 00:31:53.812
<i>She filled the skies
with Airbenders.</i>

548
00:31:54.513 --> 00:31:55.948
<i>and we flew by her side.</i>

549
00:31:56.082 --> 00:31:58.317
<i>spreading peace
across the world.</i>

550
00:32:01.420 --> 00:32:03.022
(PANTING)

551
00:32:07.126 --> 00:32:10.696
Aang? Are you okay?

552
00:32:10.796 --> 00:32:13.632
Sonam used the staff
to give people airbending.

553
00:32:14.466 --> 00:32:15.867
If we found it...

554
00:32:17.636 --> 00:32:20.339
I could bring airbending
back to the world!

555
00:32:20.506 --> 00:32:21.807
(CHUCKLES)
This is incredible!

556
00:32:21.974 --> 00:32:24.643
There haven't been Airbenders
for over a hundred years!

557
00:32:25.377 --> 00:32:28.480
This is everything
you ever wanted. Aang.

558
00:32:29.815 --> 00:32:31.984
We could heal
the greatest atrocity

559
00:32:32.118 --> 00:32:33.986
my nation committed
in the war.

560
00:32:34.786 --> 00:32:37.789
This could be the final step
to rebuilding the world.

561
00:32:37.923 --> 00:32:41.493
Not if the Denied
get there first.
They have the map.

562
00:32:42.428 --> 00:32:43.629
Who are the Denied?

563
00:32:43.762 --> 00:32:45.931
A group of violent Nonbenders.

564
00:32:46.032 --> 00:32:47.133
They...

565
00:32:47.499 --> 00:32:50.036
They must be after the staff
to give themselves airbending.

566
00:32:50.202 --> 00:32:54.240
Then there's no time to waste.
There's only one place
it could be.

567
00:32:54.340 --> 00:32:55.507
Ready your bison.

568
00:32:55.674 --> 00:32:57.809
We'll need to travel
across the endless ocean.

569
00:32:57.943 --> 00:33:01.247
On the other side of the world?
But there's nothing out there.

570
00:33:01.347 --> 00:33:02.848
There's an island.

571
00:33:03.015 --> 00:33:05.017
The journey will not be easy.

572
00:33:05.151 --> 00:33:06.585
But we can make it.

573
00:33:07.553 --> 00:33:09.088
Then let's get going.

574
00:33:09.188 --> 00:33:10.289
(CHUCKLES)

575
00:33:10.422 --> 00:33:13.025
The skies are no place
for a water child.

576
00:33:13.159 --> 00:33:14.360
Water child?

577
00:33:14.860 --> 00:33:18.564
Um. I know you just woke up
after thousands of years.

578
00:33:18.730 --> 00:33:20.566
but we do
these things together.

579
00:33:20.699 --> 00:33:23.135
Trust me.
We're stronger this way.

580
00:33:23.235 --> 00:33:24.936
Welcome to Team Avatar.

581
00:33:25.471 --> 00:33:26.772
What's your name?

582
00:33:27.473 --> 00:33:28.674
Tagah.

583
00:33:28.807 --> 00:33:30.442
My name is Tagah.

584
00:33:40.086 --> 00:33:43.155
Just think of it
as a big metal air bison.

585
00:33:50.896 --> 00:33:54.233
TAGAH: <i>We will travel
ancient paths through the sky.</i>

586
00:33:55.667 --> 00:33:56.902
<i>Ones that our people learned</i>

587
00:33:57.069 --> 00:33:59.371
<i>by following
the great air bison herds</i>

588
00:33:59.505 --> 00:34:01.573
<i>that long ago
taught us airbending.</i>

589
00:34:02.341 --> 00:34:04.042
<i>Air currents known only to us.</i>

590
00:34:04.810 --> 00:34:08.013
<i>encircling the great sphere
of existence.</i>

591
00:34:08.514 --> 00:34:10.749
<i>allowing us to travel
where we wish.</i>

592
00:34:11.350 --> 00:34:15.454
<i>giving us our name.
the Air Nomads.</i>

593
00:34:16.588 --> 00:34:17.523
(KATARA GASPS)

594
00:34:17.689 --> 00:34:20.792
(MAJESTIC MUSIC PLAYING)

595
00:34:44.983 --> 00:34:46.718
ZUKO: What's he doing?

596
00:34:47.253 --> 00:34:48.954
He's really feeling that air.

597
00:34:49.087 --> 00:34:51.823
He's navigating by instinct.

598
00:34:51.957 --> 00:34:54.059
What if his instincts
are just wrong?

599
00:34:54.160 --> 00:34:56.628
Who needs instincts
when you've got
muscles like that?

600
00:34:56.762 --> 00:34:59.465
Or what if
his brain is messed up
from being frozen?

601
00:34:59.598 --> 00:35:02.434
Like me?
Uh. no. no!

602
00:35:02.568 --> 00:35:05.137
He was frozen for
five thousand years. okay?

603
00:35:05.304 --> 00:35:07.339
You were frozen for.
what. a hundred?

604
00:35:07.506 --> 00:35:09.708
Okay. that's nothing.
Your brain is...

605
00:35:10.642 --> 00:35:11.943
fresh.

606
00:35:12.178 --> 00:35:15.113
Maybe he is
a little old-fashioned.
but look at him.

607
00:35:15.314 --> 00:35:16.815
He's so in tune
with his element.

608
00:35:16.948 --> 00:35:19.785
he can travel
across the entire ocean

609
00:35:19.918 --> 00:35:22.221
with no map.
no instruments.

610
00:35:23.989 --> 00:35:26.992
(EXHALES)
There's so much
I can learn from him.

611
00:35:32.331 --> 00:35:33.899
(SNORING)

612
00:35:35.634 --> 00:35:37.503
(APPA PURRING)
(CHUCKLES)

613
00:35:38.504 --> 00:35:42.007
I'd give anything to be able
to see my air bison again.

614
00:35:42.974 --> 00:35:44.876
(GROWLS)

615
00:35:45.544 --> 00:35:49.215
And now.
to see only one remains.

616
00:35:51.317 --> 00:35:55.454
Aang. you said our people
were wiped out.

617
00:35:55.954 --> 00:35:57.389
yet you survived.

618
00:35:57.889 --> 00:35:59.024
How?

619
00:36:00.726 --> 00:36:03.229
I had just found out
I was the Avatar.

620
00:36:03.862 --> 00:36:07.833
But the responsibility.
it was too much.

621
00:36:09.568 --> 00:36:11.036
So I ran away.

622
00:36:12.037 --> 00:36:15.707
And while I was gone.
the Fire Nation attacked.

623
00:36:18.009 --> 00:36:19.611
They were looking for me.

624
00:36:21.413 --> 00:36:22.614
If...

625
00:36:23.415 --> 00:36:24.983
If I'd just been there.

626
00:36:25.417 --> 00:36:26.852
TAGAH: Sonam would say.

627
00:36:26.985 --> 00:36:29.721
Air Nomads are formed
from the mist.

628
00:36:30.289 --> 00:36:32.758
We walk the world
for a moment in time.

629
00:36:33.259 --> 00:36:36.728
then we return
to the eternal wind.

630
00:36:38.063 --> 00:36:39.931
Monk Gyatso taught me that.

631
00:36:40.832 --> 00:36:42.601
We carry the same weight.

632
00:36:42.734 --> 00:36:45.704
a grief no one else
could possibly comprehend.

633
00:36:45.837 --> 00:36:48.740
But you and I
can heal the past.

634
00:36:49.241 --> 00:36:52.744
Let me show you how powerful
our element can be

635
00:36:52.878 --> 00:36:55.046
when Airbenders work together.

636
00:36:58.183 --> 00:36:59.985
Tagah. what are you doing?

637
00:37:00.085 --> 00:37:01.253
Whoa!

638
00:37:01.387 --> 00:37:03.221
This is how Sonam taught me.

639
00:37:03.355 --> 00:37:05.791
Feel the energy that tethers us.

640
00:37:06.458 --> 00:37:07.826
(GASPS)

641
00:37:07.926 --> 00:37:08.860
(SIGHS)

642
00:37:08.960 --> 00:37:09.995
(GROWLS PLAYFULLY)

643
00:37:10.095 --> 00:37:11.430
(LAUGHS)

644
00:37:11.563 --> 00:37:14.433
TAGAH: The bond between us.
Can you feel it?

645
00:37:14.566 --> 00:37:15.567
Use it!

646
00:37:15.701 --> 00:37:17.168
This is amazing!

647
00:37:18.169 --> 00:37:19.838
Yeah! (LAUGHS)

648
00:37:20.439 --> 00:37:21.507
(CHUCKLES)

649
00:37:22.408 --> 00:37:23.809
Woo-hoo!

650
00:37:23.975 --> 00:37:26.278
Oh. yeah!
Human boomerang!

651
00:37:26.412 --> 00:37:27.579
He's actually flying.

652
00:37:27.713 --> 00:37:28.780
TOPH: So are we.

653
00:37:28.947 --> 00:37:31.450
Whoa. that's my best friend!
That's my best friend!

654
00:37:32.618 --> 00:37:34.119
Now you throw me!

655
00:37:34.786 --> 00:37:36.154
(GRUNTING)

656
00:37:36.288 --> 00:37:39.358
(EPIC MUSIC PLAYING)

657
00:37:46.097 --> 00:37:47.333
(GRUNTS)

658
00:38:02.581 --> 00:38:04.716
I had no idea
this was possible!

659
00:38:04.816 --> 00:38:06.852
This is only the beginning.

660
00:38:14.192 --> 00:38:15.794
AANG: I can't believe it.

661
00:38:16.294 --> 00:38:18.296
Airbenders will fill
the sky again.

662
00:38:18.697 --> 00:38:20.899
TAGAH: We have been
given a great gift.

663
00:38:21.333 --> 00:38:23.201
The chance to redeem ourselves.

664
00:38:23.935 --> 00:38:26.938
You were destined to find me
on that mountain. Aang.

665
00:38:28.774 --> 00:38:30.742
How did you end up there?

666
00:38:34.380 --> 00:38:36.648
The Earthbenders
had attacked Jharana.

667
00:38:37.248 --> 00:38:39.951
Sonam and I fought fearlessly.
side by side.

668
00:38:40.486 --> 00:38:42.688
We drove them
back to Mount Baihu.

669
00:38:42.821 --> 00:38:45.023
and that's the last
I remember.

670
00:38:46.692 --> 00:38:48.360
She must have saved your life.

671
00:38:48.794 --> 00:38:51.597
Only an Avatar could have
put you in that sphere.

672
00:38:55.200 --> 00:38:58.303
Aang. can I ask you something?

673
00:38:58.437 --> 00:38:59.405
Of course.

674
00:38:59.805 --> 00:39:02.708
If the Fire Nation
destroyed the Air Nomads...

675
00:39:03.509 --> 00:39:06.478
how can you suffer
the presence of the Fire Lord?

676
00:39:06.778 --> 00:39:09.047
(PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING)

677
00:39:09.448 --> 00:39:11.316
Zuko is a friend and an ally.

678
00:39:11.817 --> 00:39:14.786
He turned against
his own father
to help me end the war.

679
00:39:14.886 --> 00:39:17.823
Yet he wears
the crown himself now.

680
00:39:18.824 --> 00:39:21.427
Fire by its nature burns. Aang.

681
00:39:22.227 --> 00:39:26.097
Our kind have always
suffered at the hands
of the other elements.

682
00:39:27.433 --> 00:39:29.267
That's why
we built Republic City.

683
00:39:29.768 --> 00:39:32.237
To show the world that
if we listen to each other.

684
00:39:32.370 --> 00:39:34.540
we can all live
together in peace.

685
00:39:34.673 --> 00:39:36.141
(MUSIC TURNS HOPEFUL)

686
00:39:36.241 --> 00:39:38.477
And once
we bring back Airbenders.

687
00:39:39.210 --> 00:39:40.646
it'll be complete.

688
00:39:43.749 --> 00:39:45.851
When everyone stuck
to their own.

689
00:39:45.984 --> 00:39:48.420
the whole world
was nearly torn apart.

690
00:39:49.187 --> 00:39:53.592
And besides. Katara.
Sokka. Zuko. Toph...

691
00:39:53.725 --> 00:39:55.326
they're my family now.

692
00:39:56.428 --> 00:39:59.598
I want to live in a world
where we can all be together.

693
00:40:00.932 --> 00:40:03.469
You remind me so much of Sonam.

694
00:40:08.073 --> 00:40:09.307
KALLIK: It's the Avatar.

695
00:40:09.475 --> 00:40:11.843
And this time he's got
his friends with him.

696
00:40:11.943 --> 00:40:13.479
That's the Fire Lord's airship!

697
00:40:13.645 --> 00:40:16.114
How'd they get ahead of us?
They don't even have the map!

698
00:40:16.615 --> 00:40:18.617
We can't risk him
getting to the staff first.

699
00:40:18.784 --> 00:40:19.651
Kill him.

700
00:40:19.818 --> 00:40:21.119
But he spared our lives.

701
00:40:21.887 --> 00:40:24.155
And how many countless were
killed in the hundred years

702
00:40:24.322 --> 00:40:25.423
waiting for his return?

703
00:40:25.624 --> 00:40:28.126
Where was he when
your family was wiped out?

704
00:40:28.259 --> 00:40:29.661
If we want anything to change.

705
00:40:29.828 --> 00:40:32.798
we need what
the Benders have... Power.

706
00:40:32.931 --> 00:40:35.033
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

707
00:40:41.172 --> 00:40:42.373
Fire!

708
00:40:43.942 --> 00:40:45.176
(BOTH GRUNT)

709
00:40:45.310 --> 00:40:47.813
(AIR WHOOSHING)
(METALLIC CLANGING)

710
00:40:47.946 --> 00:40:49.481
It's the Denied!

711
00:40:51.983 --> 00:40:54.219
Uh. we are definitely
under attack!

712
00:40:55.821 --> 00:40:57.388
Tear them to shreds!

713
00:40:58.857 --> 00:41:00.526
(AIR HISSING)

714
00:41:07.165 --> 00:41:09.200
(CLANKING)

715
00:41:10.301 --> 00:41:12.170
Is he crushing the ship?

716
00:41:14.272 --> 00:41:15.340
Tagah?

717
00:41:16.174 --> 00:41:17.342
Tagah. stop!

718
00:41:17.475 --> 00:41:18.710
(GRUNTS)

719
00:41:22.147 --> 00:41:24.049
(GRUNTING)

720
00:41:24.716 --> 00:41:25.917
(ALL GRUNT)

721
00:41:26.017 --> 00:41:27.519
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

722
00:41:27.919 --> 00:41:30.889
(MUSIC INTENSIFIES)

723
00:41:42.634 --> 00:41:43.902
We're here.

724
00:41:45.837 --> 00:41:47.739
The Immortal Storm.

725
00:41:48.239 --> 00:41:49.174
Oh. no.

726
00:41:49.307 --> 00:41:51.342
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

727
00:41:51.476 --> 00:41:54.145
(TORNADOS ROARING)

728
00:41:54.546 --> 00:41:57.182
There has to be
another way around.
No!

729
00:41:57.315 --> 00:41:59.751
Together. you and I
can clear a path for the ship.

730
00:41:59.918 --> 00:42:01.286
But we have to go now.

731
00:42:02.153 --> 00:42:04.355
Aang. trust me.

732
00:42:04.489 --> 00:42:05.824
(MOMO SCREECHES)

733
00:42:05.924 --> 00:42:07.392
(APPA MOANS)

734
00:42:07.559 --> 00:42:09.561
Uh. maybe now's
a good time to turn back.

735
00:42:09.728 --> 00:42:12.263
ZUKO: I don't think
that's an option anymore.

736
00:42:12.397 --> 00:42:13.732
Where are they going?

737
00:42:15.400 --> 00:42:16.735
(ALL GRUNT)

738
00:42:19.170 --> 00:42:20.471
(AIR HISSING)

739
00:42:22.273 --> 00:42:24.676
The engine's out.
We're losing air pressure.

740
00:42:26.544 --> 00:42:27.779
ALL: Whoa!

741
00:42:30.215 --> 00:42:32.684
Katara. Toph. come with me.
What about me?

742
00:42:32.818 --> 00:42:33.885
Take the wheel.

743
00:42:34.252 --> 00:42:36.822
What? No. I've only ever
crashed Fire Nation airships.

744
00:42:38.223 --> 00:42:39.758
Okay. let's see.
Here's our rudder.

745
00:42:39.891 --> 00:42:41.359
this is the elevator.
there's our ballast.

746
00:42:41.492 --> 00:42:44.129
and there's the giant tornado
that's going to kill us all.

747
00:42:46.564 --> 00:42:47.565
(GRUNTS)

748
00:42:47.699 --> 00:42:49.167
Follow my lead.

749
00:42:51.870 --> 00:42:53.038
(GRUNTS)

750
00:42:56.374 --> 00:42:58.243
(MUSIC SOFTENS)
(GASPS. STRAINS)

751
00:43:00.211 --> 00:43:02.748
Work with me.
just like I showed you.

752
00:43:03.481 --> 00:43:05.216
We can harness the air.

753
00:43:08.654 --> 00:43:11.623
(BOTH GRUNTING)

754
00:43:13.792 --> 00:43:14.760
(WHOOSHES)

755
00:43:15.493 --> 00:43:17.696
(MUSIC INTENSIFIES)
Yes! That's it. Aang!
Keep going!

756
00:43:27.773 --> 00:43:29.975
ZUKO: There's a long tear
above your head on the left.

757
00:43:30.108 --> 00:43:31.142
Got it!

758
00:43:31.476 --> 00:43:34.145
ZUKO: Whatever happens.
you have to hold
the ship together.

759
00:43:34.312 --> 00:43:35.947
SOKKA: <i>Zuko! Zuko!</i>

760
00:43:36.081 --> 00:43:38.049
Aang and Tagah
are destroying tornadoes.

761
00:43:38.149 --> 00:43:40.786
but there's too many.
and they're everywhere!

762
00:43:40.919 --> 00:43:42.988
Just steer the ship.
Don't lose Aang.

763
00:43:43.154 --> 00:43:44.289
It's not that easy.

764
00:43:44.422 --> 00:43:46.692
especially when
everything is sideways.

765
00:43:46.858 --> 00:43:48.493
Okay. left!

766
00:43:48.626 --> 00:43:50.161
(PANTING)

767
00:43:51.930 --> 00:43:53.198
(METAL CREAKS)

768
00:43:56.702 --> 00:43:58.770
(LAUGHS) I did it!

769
00:43:58.904 --> 00:44:00.872
(YELPS) Right!

770
00:44:08.880 --> 00:44:11.049
Oh. no!
We're falling behind!

771
00:44:12.017 --> 00:44:14.720
I'm losing sight of them!
We have to go back!

772
00:44:14.853 --> 00:44:16.021
Trust in your friends.

773
00:44:16.154 --> 00:44:18.757
They won't make it
if we don't clear a path.

774
00:44:22.293 --> 00:44:23.461
(WHOOSHES)

775
00:44:27.198 --> 00:44:29.735
(METAL CREAKS)

776
00:44:31.737 --> 00:44:33.872
Zuko! We're gonna
crash into the sea!

777
00:44:34.039 --> 00:44:37.542
When I give you the signal.
pull the lever
next to the wheel.

778
00:44:40.345 --> 00:44:41.412
(RATTLING)

779
00:44:41.847 --> 00:44:43.749
SOKKA:
We're gonna crash!
We're gonna crash!

780
00:44:44.015 --> 00:44:45.150
Katara?

781
00:44:48.887 --> 00:44:49.888
(GRUNTS)

782
00:44:50.021 --> 00:44:52.557
(EPIC MUSIC PLAYING)

783
00:45:02.400 --> 00:45:04.602
(SCREAMS)

784
00:45:04.770 --> 00:45:06.604
Give me the signal!
Give me the signal!

785
00:45:11.276 --> 00:45:12.510
It's closed!

786
00:45:13.945 --> 00:45:15.346
Sokka. now!

787
00:45:15.446 --> 00:45:16.748
Here we go!

788
00:45:16.882 --> 00:45:17.783
(GRUNTS)

789
00:45:35.466 --> 00:45:37.302
(MUSIC FADES)

790
00:45:39.470 --> 00:45:41.672
AANG: Katara! We did it!

791
00:45:42.573 --> 00:45:44.109
What were you thinking?

792
00:45:44.242 --> 00:45:45.576
I was clearing the tornadoes
to make a path.

793
00:45:45.710 --> 00:45:47.813
The ship almost crashed. Aang.
We could have died.

794
00:45:47.979 --> 00:45:50.281
(DARK PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING)
And what if you
got yourself killed?

795
00:45:50.448 --> 00:45:51.449
You're the Avatar.

796
00:45:51.582 --> 00:45:54.252
This is too risky.
We need to turn back now.

797
00:45:54.385 --> 00:45:56.621
No! We're almost there.

798
00:45:56.754 --> 00:45:59.624
We just need to get
to the eye of the storm.

799
00:46:00.225 --> 00:46:02.660
Aang. no.
This is too dangerous.

800
00:46:02.828 --> 00:46:05.430
The staff is out there.
The Denied are after it.

801
00:46:05.563 --> 00:46:08.199
Do you really believe
that they could make it
through the storm?

802
00:46:08.299 --> 00:46:09.400
We're nearly there.

803
00:46:09.534 --> 00:46:11.469
That staff
can bring back my people.

804
00:46:11.602 --> 00:46:12.904
I understand how much
you want that. but...

805
00:46:13.038 --> 00:46:15.340
You don't understand.
None of you do.

806
00:46:16.574 --> 00:46:17.976
Aang...

807
00:46:19.878 --> 00:46:20.846
We push forward.

808
00:46:24.615 --> 00:46:27.853
TAGAH:
If we generate enough air.
we can push our way through.

809
00:46:32.924 --> 00:46:35.393
(BOTH GRUNTING)

810
00:46:36.127 --> 00:46:39.564
(MUSIC BUILDS DRAMATICALLY)

811
00:46:46.838 --> 00:46:47.873
(BOTH GRUNT)

812
00:47:00.651 --> 00:47:02.387
(ALL YELP)

813
00:47:10.761 --> 00:47:11.629
(MUSIC FADES)

814
00:47:11.762 --> 00:47:13.865
(PANTING)
We're alive?

815
00:47:14.465 --> 00:47:17.035
We made it through.
Thank you. Tagah.

816
00:47:17.168 --> 00:47:19.871
It was you. Aang.
We're here because of you.

817
00:47:20.038 --> 00:47:21.672
Yeah. we're having
a good time. too.

818
00:47:21.873 --> 00:47:24.209
You could have told us
we were flying into
the Immortal Storm.

819
00:47:24.375 --> 00:47:26.978
I know it was dangerous.
but we had to risk it.

820
00:47:27.112 --> 00:47:28.179
We? (CHUCKLES)

821
00:47:28.313 --> 00:47:30.315
I don't remember when
we took a vote on that.

822
00:47:30.448 --> 00:47:32.583
There wasn't time.
I had to make a call.

823
00:47:32.717 --> 00:47:34.552
TAGAH: Friends. please.
don't blame Aang.

824
00:47:34.685 --> 00:47:36.287
This is all my fault.
(GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING)

825
00:47:36.387 --> 00:47:38.123
I knew this would be difficult.

826
00:47:38.890 --> 00:47:41.526
But Aang believed
in your strength as a team.

827
00:47:41.659 --> 00:47:43.794
And I'm honored
to be a part of it.

828
00:47:49.767 --> 00:47:51.402
I forgive you. Tagah.

829
00:47:51.836 --> 00:47:53.604
AANG: Everyone. look.

830
00:47:54.872 --> 00:47:59.144
These islands.
they were Lion Turtles.

831
00:48:01.012 --> 00:48:02.113
Whoa.

832
00:48:03.448 --> 00:48:04.950
KATARA: It's beautiful.

833
00:48:05.116 --> 00:48:06.918
(BIRDS CAWING)

834
00:48:07.252 --> 00:48:08.954
Long before my time.

835
00:48:09.087 --> 00:48:10.855
the Lion Turtles
granted the gift

836
00:48:10.989 --> 00:48:12.590
of bending to humans.

837
00:48:13.158 --> 00:48:16.027
These are their final
resting grounds.

838
00:48:16.127 --> 00:48:19.464
This is where Sonam came
to learn their ways.

839
00:48:20.131 --> 00:48:23.601
I am certain that
she left her staff here.

840
00:48:23.768 --> 00:48:25.270
Where should we start looking?

841
00:48:25.436 --> 00:48:28.273
Aang. you must
connect with her.

842
00:48:28.940 --> 00:48:31.842
But no one
can connect with Sonam.

843
00:48:31.943 --> 00:48:33.945
TAGAH: The spiritual power
of the Lion Turtles

844
00:48:34.112 --> 00:48:35.846
is still
concentrated here.

845
00:48:35.947 --> 00:48:37.515
Let it guide you.

846
00:48:37.949 --> 00:48:39.350
We'll set out immediately.

847
00:48:39.517 --> 00:48:42.387
Actually. Tagah.
we could really
use your help here.

848
00:48:42.487 --> 00:48:45.590
If the Denied are close behind.
we need to be ready.

849
00:48:45.723 --> 00:48:48.426
Yeah. and we're gonna need more
than Toph's metal bending

850
00:48:48.559 --> 00:48:49.594
to fix this ship.

851
00:48:49.794 --> 00:48:51.629
My bending got us
through that storm.

852
00:48:51.762 --> 00:48:52.797
What did you do?

853
00:48:52.964 --> 00:48:54.099
Steered with his feet.

854
00:48:54.232 --> 00:48:55.566
Repairs can wait.

855
00:48:55.666 --> 00:48:56.867
Aang needs me.

856
00:48:57.035 --> 00:49:00.805
Tagah. please.
stay and help my friends.

857
00:49:01.306 --> 00:49:03.008
I'll be okay on my own.

858
00:49:03.608 --> 00:49:04.709
As you wish.

859
00:49:05.076 --> 00:49:07.979
We will begin repairs
for our voyage home.

860
00:49:09.814 --> 00:49:13.584
AANG: Everyone. I know
I've asked a lot of you
on this journey.

861
00:49:13.718 --> 00:49:15.953
but we're about
to accomplish something

862
00:49:16.087 --> 00:49:17.989
that will change the world.

863
00:49:19.257 --> 00:49:20.691
(WHISTLE BLOWS)

864
00:49:20.858 --> 00:49:23.894
(HOPEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

865
00:49:23.995 --> 00:49:25.430
(APPA GROWLING)

866
00:49:34.605 --> 00:49:36.441
(CAWING)

867
00:50:09.340 --> 00:50:11.076
Let it guide you.

868
00:50:27.258 --> 00:50:28.726
Sonam?

869
00:50:46.644 --> 00:50:50.415
Oh. this is turning out to be
a nice little vacation. (SIGHS)

870
00:50:50.581 --> 00:50:52.983
Aside from all the people
trying to kill us.

871
00:50:53.084 --> 00:50:53.918
And the tornadoes.

872
00:50:54.319 --> 00:50:56.554
Um. we're supposed
to be fixing the ship?

873
00:50:56.687 --> 00:50:58.389
SOKKA:
You're doing great. buddy.

874
00:50:58.523 --> 00:51:00.691
(GROANS)
KATARA: Has anyone seen Tagah?

875
00:51:00.791 --> 00:51:02.427
Yes. we've all seen Tagah.

876
00:51:02.593 --> 00:51:05.130
He's so gorgeous.
Jeez. I get it.

877
00:51:05.763 --> 00:51:06.964
Oh. I see what you mean.

878
00:51:07.132 --> 00:51:08.766
He wandered off that way.

879
00:51:08.933 --> 00:51:11.202
No. maybe that way?

880
00:51:44.969 --> 00:51:46.204
KATARA: Tagah!

881
00:51:46.671 --> 00:51:48.539
Where are you going?

882
00:51:48.639 --> 00:51:50.375
Aang needs to be protected.

883
00:51:50.941 --> 00:51:52.143
I agree.

884
00:51:54.645 --> 00:51:57.482
I know my ways
may seem unusual to you.

885
00:51:57.615 --> 00:52:00.585
but I assure you.
everything I do.

886
00:52:00.685 --> 00:52:01.919
I do for Aang.

887
00:52:02.052 --> 00:52:04.822
For Aang?
Or for the staff?

888
00:52:05.990 --> 00:52:08.693
You have no idea
all that we've lost.

889
00:52:08.826 --> 00:52:11.262
You've never known
a world with Airbenders.

890
00:52:11.929 --> 00:52:13.498
I know Aang.

891
00:52:14.131 --> 00:52:16.000
<i>He may be the last of his kind.</i>

892
00:52:16.167 --> 00:52:18.669
<i>but he's the reason
this world knows peace.</i>

893
00:52:18.936 --> 00:52:21.672
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

894
00:52:22.373 --> 00:52:26.311
<i>His values as an Air Nomad
have brought balance to chaos.</i>

895
00:52:28.613 --> 00:52:31.816
<i>It's because of Aang
that the Water Tribes.</i>

896
00:52:31.949 --> 00:52:35.486
<i>Earth Kingdom. and Fire Nation
now work together.</i>

897
00:52:35.620 --> 00:52:37.522
<i>striving for harmony.</i>

898
00:52:37.688 --> 00:52:40.291
<i>a peace we once
thought unattainable.</i>

899
00:52:42.827 --> 00:52:44.362
TAGAH: <i>You speak of peace.</i>

900
00:52:44.529 --> 00:52:47.532
There will never be peace
among the elements.

901
00:52:47.698 --> 00:52:48.833
<i>There never was.</i>

902
00:52:49.133 --> 00:52:52.069
<i>Your precious Republic City
is built on lies.</i>

903
00:52:52.203 --> 00:52:54.372
KATARA:
<i>It's built on hope.</i>

904
00:52:54.539 --> 00:52:55.906
<i>Do you have hope. Tagah?</i>

905
00:52:56.040 --> 00:52:59.076
Saving my people requires
more than just hope.

906
00:52:59.244 --> 00:53:00.911
It requires sacrifice.

907
00:53:01.078 --> 00:53:04.048
I saw you try to crush
the Denied's airships.

908
00:53:04.181 --> 00:53:05.883
You were ready to kill them.

909
00:53:08.085 --> 00:53:10.888
<i>I know what kind
of Airbender Aang is...</i>

910
00:53:13.358 --> 00:53:15.593
but what kind
of Airbender are you?

911
00:53:16.761 --> 00:53:19.797
(AIR WHOOSHING)

912
00:53:25.570 --> 00:53:28.306
(RUMBLING)

913
00:53:44.188 --> 00:53:46.023
TAGAH: Aang did well
getting us here.

914
00:53:46.457 --> 00:53:50.227
There is great strength in him.
but weakness as well.

915
00:53:50.361 --> 00:53:51.496
Weakness?

916
00:53:51.596 --> 00:53:52.863
TAGAH: Yes.

917
00:53:52.963 --> 00:53:54.031
You.

918
00:53:54.131 --> 00:53:56.166
(BOTH GRUNTING)

919
00:53:59.404 --> 00:54:00.938
(ICE CRACKLING)
(GASPS)

920
00:54:04.942 --> 00:54:06.311
(GRUNTS)

921
00:54:10.581 --> 00:54:11.716
What the hog monkey?

922
00:54:11.816 --> 00:54:13.484
(GRUNTS)

923
00:54:15.653 --> 00:54:16.687
No!

924
00:54:19.990 --> 00:54:21.926
(GLOWING LIGHT HUMMING)

925
00:54:23.160 --> 00:54:25.863
(TWINKLING)

926
00:54:27.832 --> 00:54:30.368
(BOTH GRUNTING)

927
00:54:35.406 --> 00:54:37.074
He trusted you!

928
00:54:39.243 --> 00:54:40.511
(GRUNTS)

929
00:54:44.014 --> 00:54:45.182
No.

930
00:54:47.585 --> 00:54:48.653
(ICE CRACKLING)

931
00:54:48.819 --> 00:54:50.355
ZUKO: You traitor!
(BOOMERANG WHOOSHING)

932
00:54:50.655 --> 00:54:52.390
(ALL GRUNTING)

933
00:54:53.958 --> 00:54:55.726
(YELLING)

934
00:54:56.861 --> 00:55:01.332
(ALL GRUNTING)

935
00:55:04.469 --> 00:55:05.403
(SHOUTS)

936
00:55:29.727 --> 00:55:30.828
(GASPS)

937
00:55:31.896 --> 00:55:33.564
(GROANS)

938
00:55:34.365 --> 00:55:35.800
(GRUNTS)

939
00:55:38.235 --> 00:55:39.570
Tagah!

940
00:55:41.305 --> 00:55:42.407
(GRUNTS)

941
00:55:43.374 --> 00:55:45.976
(MUSIC INTENSIFIES)

942
00:55:47.578 --> 00:55:49.747
(AIR WHOOSHING)

943
00:55:55.586 --> 00:55:58.055
(MUSIC SOFTENS)

944
00:56:05.463 --> 00:56:06.597
TAGAH: Brother.

945
00:56:09.500 --> 00:56:11.836
Tagah. It's real.

946
00:56:16.173 --> 00:56:18.643
We can finally
bring back airbending.

947
00:56:21.779 --> 00:56:23.047
Let's go tell the others.

948
00:56:23.180 --> 00:56:24.449
We can do this.

949
00:56:25.115 --> 00:56:26.451
Me and you.

950
00:56:27.084 --> 00:56:29.153
I can't do this
without my friends.

951
00:56:31.255 --> 00:56:34.324
Earth killed my people.
Fire killed yours.

952
00:56:34.425 --> 00:56:38.463
The staff is the only way
we can create a new Air Empire.

953
00:56:38.596 --> 00:56:40.931
One capable of defending itself.

954
00:56:41.065 --> 00:56:42.099
No.

955
00:56:42.232 --> 00:56:44.234
We can build
a new future. Tagah.

956
00:56:44.368 --> 00:56:46.303
But it has to be for everyone.

957
00:56:46.471 --> 00:56:48.606
The staff doesn't
belong to everyone.

958
00:56:48.739 --> 00:56:49.874
It belongs to us.

959
00:56:50.007 --> 00:56:51.809
What...
What have you done?

960
00:56:51.976 --> 00:56:55.713
TAGAH: As long as they were
around. you'd always put them
ahead of our people.

961
00:56:55.813 --> 00:56:59.349
Don't you see?
This is how we redeem ourselves.

962
00:56:59.950 --> 00:57:01.719
It doesn't matter
that you ran then.

963
00:57:01.819 --> 00:57:03.821
As long as you stand
with me now.

964
00:57:03.988 --> 00:57:06.824
No... Katara.
TAGAH: Aang. listen to me.

965
00:57:06.957 --> 00:57:08.325
This is the only way.

966
00:57:08.493 --> 00:57:11.361
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

967
00:57:12.096 --> 00:57:13.430
(SHOUTS)

968
00:57:22.139 --> 00:57:24.074
You're a traitor to your own.

969
00:57:24.174 --> 00:57:26.343
Just like Sonam.

970
00:57:29.947 --> 00:57:31.549
(SHOUTS)

971
00:57:32.817 --> 00:57:34.051
(GRUNTS)

972
00:57:35.853 --> 00:57:37.555
(APPA ROARS)

973
00:57:45.596 --> 00:57:47.164
(SHOUTS)

974
00:57:49.333 --> 00:57:51.368
(MUSIC ENDS ABRUPTLY)

975
00:57:51.602 --> 00:57:53.337
(GROANS)

976
00:57:59.777 --> 00:58:02.079
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)
(APPA MOANING)

977
00:58:04.014 --> 00:58:06.584
TAGAH: I wanted to do this
with you by my side.

978
00:58:07.518 --> 00:58:10.220
But if I must build
the new Air Empire alone...

979
00:58:11.288 --> 00:58:12.590
so be it.

980
00:58:15.860 --> 00:58:17.562
(MOANS)

981
00:58:20.631 --> 00:58:23.868
There's no way in!
We have to turn back!
(STRAINING)

982
00:58:24.001 --> 00:58:27.037
No! We keep trying
to push through!

983
00:58:39.416 --> 00:58:41.118
Sonam's staff.

984
00:58:41.986 --> 00:58:43.387
TAGAH: Denied...

985
00:58:43.520 --> 00:58:45.189
the Avatar is dead.

986
00:58:45.556 --> 00:58:48.425
If you wish to build a new world
where you have the power.

987
00:58:48.559 --> 00:58:50.327
I can give it to you.

988
00:58:52.262 --> 00:58:54.732
(MUSIC FADES)

989
00:59:00.070 --> 00:59:01.505
(AANG GRUNTS)

990
00:59:05.576 --> 00:59:06.744
Appa!

991
00:59:06.911 --> 00:59:08.545
Katara!

992
00:59:08.679 --> 00:59:10.114
Katara! (ECHOES)

993
00:59:11.415 --> 00:59:12.650
Katara.

994
00:59:13.283 --> 00:59:14.652
They're gone.

995
00:59:15.219 --> 00:59:16.754
It's all my fault.

996
00:59:17.588 --> 00:59:19.289
It's always been my fault.

997
00:59:19.790 --> 00:59:21.759
Ever since I ran away.

998
00:59:23.327 --> 00:59:26.797
SONAM: No Avatar has ever
fallen into such shame

999
00:59:26.964 --> 00:59:29.199
as to join me
here in my sorrow.

1000
00:59:31.201 --> 00:59:33.137
Why do you grieve so. friend?

1001
00:59:33.638 --> 00:59:35.673
Avatar Sonam?

1002
00:59:38.275 --> 00:59:40.144
Tagah murdered my friends.

1003
00:59:40.711 --> 00:59:42.379
And now he has the staff.

1004
00:59:42.512 --> 00:59:44.248
Tagah? No.

1005
00:59:44.381 --> 00:59:47.217
No. I... I stopped him.

1006
00:59:47.317 --> 00:59:48.786
I hid the staff.

1007
00:59:49.219 --> 00:59:51.388
What have you done?

1008
00:59:52.089 --> 00:59:54.291
You're the one
who gave him airbending!

1009
00:59:54.725 --> 00:59:57.027
How could you give power
to a monster?

1010
00:59:57.561 --> 01:00:01.298
The Tagah I gave bending to
was a different man.

1011
01:00:01.498 --> 01:00:02.733
(PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING)

1012
01:00:02.867 --> 01:00:04.635
SONAM:
<i>It was a different time.</i>

1013
01:00:05.369 --> 01:00:08.238
<i>The Airbenders were
the peacekeepers
of the four elements.</i>

1014
01:00:08.739 --> 01:00:11.308
<i>We used our power
to mediate all conflict</i>

1015
01:00:11.475 --> 01:00:12.710
<i>with non-violence.</i>

1016
01:00:13.210 --> 01:00:15.245
<i>But we were
the fewest in numbers.</i>

1017
01:00:16.146 --> 01:00:19.750
<i>For many years. we existed
in a beautiful balance</i>

1018
01:00:19.850 --> 01:00:21.418
<i>of great prosperity.</i>

1019
01:00:21.518 --> 01:00:23.420
<i>But the world began to shift.</i>

1020
01:00:24.121 --> 01:00:26.423
<i>The Earthbenders
formed their own kingdom.</i>

1021
01:00:26.556 --> 01:00:29.159
<i>separating from
the other elemental tribes.</i>

1022
01:00:29.827 --> 01:00:31.962
<i>The balance of the world
was at risk.</i>

1023
01:00:32.362 --> 01:00:34.531
<i>It was my duty to act.</i>

1024
01:00:35.532 --> 01:00:37.167
<i>So I learned how
to channel the energy</i>

1025
01:00:37.334 --> 01:00:39.904
<i>of the Spirit World
just as the Lion Turtles did.</i>

1026
01:00:40.237 --> 01:00:43.340
<i>To give people
the power of airbending.</i>

1027
01:00:44.241 --> 01:00:45.876
<i>My most devout pupil.</i>

1028
01:00:46.010 --> 01:00:48.746
<i>Tagah. was the first
to receive it.</i>

1029
01:00:49.714 --> 01:00:51.581
<i>I sent my new peacekeepers out</i>

1030
01:00:51.682 --> 01:00:53.818
<i>to help calm
the growing unrest.</i>

1031
01:00:54.618 --> 01:00:57.221
<i>But they were not prepared
for the brutality</i>

1032
01:00:57.387 --> 01:00:59.556
<i>of the new Earth Kingdom.</i>
(SCREAMS)

1033
01:01:01.458 --> 01:01:02.727
<i>Tagah watched</i>

1034
01:01:03.127 --> 01:01:06.596
<i>as his brothers and sisters
were all slaughtered.</i>

1035
01:01:07.464 --> 01:01:10.200
<i>His heart darkened
by the violence of war.</i>

1036
01:01:10.667 --> 01:01:14.972
<i>He now saw everyone
who wasn't an Air Nomad
as the enemy.</i>

1037
01:01:16.306 --> 01:01:18.575
<i>Tagah begged me to use
the staff to create an army</i>

1038
01:01:18.743 --> 01:01:21.411
<i>and to kill
all who would do us harm.</i>

1039
01:01:21.879 --> 01:01:23.347
<i>I refused.</i>

1040
01:01:23.714 --> 01:01:24.849
<i>So he stole it.</i>

1041
01:01:24.982 --> 01:01:26.050
(THUNDER CRASHES)

1042
01:01:26.550 --> 01:01:28.218
SONAM:
<i>When he connected the staff
to the temple.</i>

1043
01:01:28.352 --> 01:01:31.355
<i>his energy was so corrupted
by grief and rage</i>

1044
01:01:31.488 --> 01:01:33.390
<i>that the power
of the Spirit World</i>
(TAGAH SCREAMS)

1045
01:01:33.523 --> 01:01:34.558
<i>consumed him.</i>

1046
01:01:35.325 --> 01:01:38.528
<i>Tagah became something
more than human.</i>

1047
01:01:38.662 --> 01:01:40.164
<i>too powerful to kill.</i>

1048
01:01:41.231 --> 01:01:43.801
<i>It took all my energy
to finally trap him</i>

1049
01:01:43.901 --> 01:01:47.738
<i>high above the clouds.
where no one would find him.</i>

1050
01:01:48.638 --> 01:01:50.540
<i>I reclaimed the staff.</i>

1051
01:01:51.008 --> 01:01:52.642
<i>but I was fatally wounded.</i>

1052
01:01:53.243 --> 01:01:55.780
<i>Before the Earth Kingdom
could invade Jharana.</i>

1053
01:01:55.913 --> 01:01:58.816
<i>I sent the remaining Air Nomads
into the mountains.</i>

1054
01:01:59.683 --> 01:02:01.819
<i>And I hid my temple
in the Spirit World.</i>

1055
01:02:01.919 --> 01:02:04.421
<i>where no one
could access its power.</i>

1056
01:02:06.023 --> 01:02:08.292
<i>Then I locked the staff away.</i>

1057
01:02:08.458 --> 01:02:10.995
<i>where only the Avatar
could find it.</i>

1058
01:02:12.262 --> 01:02:14.999
<i>I died. hoping that one day.</i>

1059
01:02:15.099 --> 01:02:17.634
<i>another Avatar would
create more Airbenders</i>

1060
01:02:17.768 --> 01:02:20.137
<i>and restore balance
to this world.</i>

1061
01:02:20.871 --> 01:02:23.473
And that Avatar is you. Aang.

1062
01:02:23.607 --> 01:02:25.075
You have to get my staff

1063
01:02:25.209 --> 01:02:27.111
before Tagah connects it
to the temple.

1064
01:02:27.611 --> 01:02:29.013
There's still time.

1065
01:02:29.113 --> 01:02:31.215
Don't let my regret
become yours.

1066
01:02:31.882 --> 01:02:34.351
AANG: My friends and I
fought hard for this peace.

1067
01:02:34.751 --> 01:02:37.221
I won't let him
start another war.

1068
01:02:37.354 --> 01:02:38.956
Help me find a way back.

1069
01:02:39.089 --> 01:02:40.590
(MUSIC BUILDS
THEN STOPS ABRUPTLY)

1070
01:02:40.724 --> 01:02:41.826
AANG: Sonam?

1071
01:02:43.093 --> 01:02:44.328
What's happening?

1072
01:02:44.494 --> 01:02:45.695
(YELPS)

1073
01:02:46.496 --> 01:02:47.497
No!

1074
01:02:47.631 --> 01:02:49.233
No! Please!

1075
01:02:49.366 --> 01:02:50.534
I have to fix this!

1076
01:02:50.634 --> 01:02:53.003
This can't be it!
I can't die yet!

1077
01:02:53.137 --> 01:02:54.604
Please! Not yet!

1078
01:02:54.738 --> 01:02:56.140
No!
KATARA: <i>Aang?</i>

1079
01:02:56.273 --> 01:02:57.975
Katara?
KATARA: <i>I'm losing him.</i>

1080
01:02:58.108 --> 01:03:00.577
<i>Come on. Aang!
Come on! Aang!</i>

1081
01:03:00.677 --> 01:03:02.279
Hold on!
(GASPS)

1082
01:03:02.412 --> 01:03:03.747
Aang!

1083
01:03:04.949 --> 01:03:05.950
Katara!

1084
01:03:06.083 --> 01:03:07.417
I was so worried.

1085
01:03:07.818 --> 01:03:08.752
SOKKA: Aang!

1086
01:03:08.886 --> 01:03:10.855
AANG: Sokka!
(SOKKA SIGHS)

1087
01:03:10.988 --> 01:03:12.389
I knew you'd
pull through. buddy.

1088
01:03:12.489 --> 01:03:13.423
Hey. Aang.

1089
01:03:13.523 --> 01:03:14.758
Zuko!

1090
01:03:14.859 --> 01:03:16.126
(CHITTERS)
Momo!

1091
01:03:16.626 --> 01:03:18.328
Welcome back. twinkle toes.

1092
01:03:18.462 --> 01:03:20.264
Toph. you're okay.

1093
01:03:20.397 --> 01:03:21.631
I...

1094
01:03:21.765 --> 01:03:23.000
I thought you were all dead.

1095
01:03:23.133 --> 01:03:26.270
We were.
But Katara saved us.

1096
01:03:26.370 --> 01:03:28.272
<i>The spiritual power
of these waters</i>

1097
01:03:28.405 --> 01:03:30.674
<i>strengthened my healing abilities.</i>

1098
01:03:33.377 --> 01:03:34.879
You're incredible. Katara.

1099
01:03:36.981 --> 01:03:38.215
Where's Appa?

1100
01:03:38.348 --> 01:03:39.383
(PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING)

1101
01:03:39.549 --> 01:03:41.218
Tagah must have taken him.

1102
01:03:41.852 --> 01:03:43.087
I'm sorry.

1103
01:03:43.553 --> 01:03:44.721
No.

1104
01:03:45.822 --> 01:03:47.925
I can't believe I trusted him.

1105
01:03:49.860 --> 01:03:51.695
KATARA:
We'll get through this.

1106
01:03:54.031 --> 01:03:55.832
SOKKA:
So. let me get this straight.

1107
01:03:55.966 --> 01:03:58.969
He's pulling Sonam's temple
out of the Spirit World

1108
01:03:59.069 --> 01:04:01.538
to gain unlimited power.
and let me guess.

1109
01:04:01.671 --> 01:04:03.240
you want us to stop him?

1110
01:04:04.141 --> 01:04:06.510
Sure. only problem
is your air bro

1111
01:04:06.643 --> 01:04:09.179
crushed our ship
and stole your bison.

1112
01:04:09.313 --> 01:04:12.616
Also. there's a massive
typhoon surrounding us!

1113
01:04:14.184 --> 01:04:15.319
(THUNDER RUMBLES)

1114
01:04:15.452 --> 01:04:18.989
I don't say this very often.
but Sokka's right.

1115
01:04:19.123 --> 01:04:21.258
Thank you.
Yep. we're stuck.

1116
01:04:21.391 --> 01:04:22.759
And there aren't
enough Lion Turtles

1117
01:04:22.893 --> 01:04:24.661
for all of us
to have our own island.

1118
01:04:24.794 --> 01:04:26.330
so I'm calling this one.

1119
01:04:26.430 --> 01:04:27.564
I'm naming him Snappy.

1120
01:04:27.697 --> 01:04:30.034
SOKKA: Aw.
Snappy is the best one.

1121
01:04:30.167 --> 01:04:31.235
TOPH: I know.

1122
01:04:31.368 --> 01:04:33.237
We may not know where Tagah is.

1123
01:04:33.737 --> 01:04:35.272
but we know
what he's looking for

1124
01:04:35.439 --> 01:04:36.740
is in the Spirit World.

1125
01:04:37.307 --> 01:04:38.742
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)
<i>And lucky for us.</i>

1126
01:04:38.909 --> 01:04:41.178
<i>we're stuck in the most
spiritually charged place</i>

1127
01:04:41.278 --> 01:04:42.279
<i>on the planet.</i>

1128
01:04:42.846 --> 01:04:45.615
<i>So I may be able to open
a portal to get us there.</i>

1129
01:04:45.782 --> 01:04:48.785
<i>if I can summon an old friend.</i>

1130
01:04:52.756 --> 01:04:53.958
(ALL YELP)

1131
01:04:57.161 --> 01:04:58.295
Wow.

1132
01:04:59.163 --> 01:05:01.431
ZUKO: The ocean spirit.

1133
01:05:01.565 --> 01:05:04.168
(MUSIC TURNS EPIC)

1134
01:05:04.935 --> 01:05:08.072
(GROWLS)

1135
01:05:08.805 --> 01:05:11.441
This portal smells an awful lot
like the fish market.

1136
01:05:11.608 --> 01:05:13.410
I'm gonna go check on Snappy.

1137
01:05:13.543 --> 01:05:15.212
Face your death with honor.

1138
01:05:15.345 --> 01:05:16.546
I'm sorry.

1139
01:05:16.646 --> 01:05:17.948
I know I got us into this.

1140
01:05:18.082 --> 01:05:20.417
but I promise you
I'll fix it.

1141
01:05:20.850 --> 01:05:22.352
KATARA: We'll fix it...

1142
01:05:22.786 --> 01:05:24.154
together.

1143
01:05:27.124 --> 01:05:29.459
SOKKA:
We're gonna die!
We're gonna die!

1144
01:05:29.593 --> 01:05:31.996
Woah!

1145
01:05:37.834 --> 01:05:39.636
(SOKKA GROANS)

1146
01:05:40.070 --> 01:05:42.006
What?
Where's my power pony?

1147
01:05:42.139 --> 01:05:44.841
Uh. were my hands
always this small?

1148
01:05:45.009 --> 01:05:46.410
(YELPS) It's Baby Toph!

1149
01:05:46.543 --> 01:05:49.246
Baby Toph!
(GRUNTING)

1150
01:05:49.379 --> 01:05:51.381
What the hog monkey?

1151
01:05:51.481 --> 01:05:52.649
(YELPS) Old people!

1152
01:05:52.782 --> 01:05:53.650
Gran Gran?

1153
01:05:53.950 --> 01:05:55.619
It's your sister.
you meathead!

1154
01:05:55.752 --> 01:05:58.088
Give me Toph.
There. there. Toph.

1155
01:05:58.222 --> 01:05:59.823
Oh. no. Zuko!

1156
01:05:59.956 --> 01:06:01.591
What happened
to your beautiful face?

1157
01:06:01.725 --> 01:06:04.561
You look like a dried sea squid.
(GROANS)

1158
01:06:04.661 --> 01:06:05.996
No. Zuko!
Tired.

1159
01:06:06.130 --> 01:06:08.298
Ow. ow. ow!
What's going on here?

1160
01:06:08.865 --> 01:06:11.235
AANG: The Spirit World
is out of balance.

1161
01:06:11.901 --> 01:06:13.537
And so are we.

1162
01:06:15.539 --> 01:06:17.074
That's gotta be Tagah.

1163
01:06:18.842 --> 01:06:21.011
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1164
01:06:38.895 --> 01:06:40.164
AANG: Oh. no!

1165
01:06:40.364 --> 01:06:42.666
He's pulling Sonam's temple
into our world!

1166
01:06:42.799 --> 01:06:44.301
We're running out of time!

1167
01:06:44.701 --> 01:06:47.437
GORILLAVARK: (YELLING) Chunder!

1168
01:06:47.837 --> 01:06:49.039
(ALL YELP)

1169
01:06:51.175 --> 01:06:52.942
(SIGHS) Pretty good landing.

1170
01:06:53.043 --> 01:06:54.144
(GROANS)

1171
01:06:54.278 --> 01:06:55.745
Whoa! Humans!

1172
01:06:55.879 --> 01:06:57.181
I love humans!

1173
01:06:57.314 --> 01:06:58.748
Two brothers.
their little sister.

1174
01:06:58.882 --> 01:07:00.084
and an elderly couple.

1175
01:07:00.250 --> 01:07:01.718
ZUKO AND KATARA: A couple?
Not a couple!

1176
01:07:01.851 --> 01:07:04.088
Whoa! Looks like
I touched a nerve.

1177
01:07:04.221 --> 01:07:06.123
Oh. look at this one.

1178
01:07:06.223 --> 01:07:07.391
Hello. Ow!

1179
01:07:07.557 --> 01:07:09.359
Toph. no! Bad Toph.

1180
01:07:09.493 --> 01:07:11.195
We don't bite strangers.

1181
01:07:11.328 --> 01:07:12.129
(YELPS)

1182
01:07:12.229 --> 01:07:13.797
AANG: Great Spirit. excuse me.

1183
01:07:13.897 --> 01:07:15.865
Did you just come from
that temple in the sky?

1184
01:07:15.999 --> 01:07:17.434
I certainly did.

1185
01:07:18.168 --> 01:07:20.637
It was my favorite hidey-hole
until that dark.

1186
01:07:20.737 --> 01:07:23.307
yucky energy started
corrupting this whole place.

1187
01:07:23.907 --> 01:07:26.976
Please. we need your help
getting up there.

1188
01:07:27.077 --> 01:07:28.912
It's my duty to stop this.

1189
01:07:29.346 --> 01:07:31.248
I'm the Avatar.
(CHITTERS)

1190
01:07:31.815 --> 01:07:34.984
Ooh. the Avatar.

1191
01:07:35.385 --> 01:07:36.653
Let me have a squiz at you.

1192
01:07:36.753 --> 01:07:39.489
Okay. Now with this eye.
And this eye.

1193
01:07:39.589 --> 01:07:41.391
Mm-hmm. And this eye.
Don't forget this eye.

1194
01:07:41.525 --> 01:07:44.361
Hey. hey. can we hurry up?
GORILLAVARK: Every eye needs
to have a squiz!

1195
01:07:44.461 --> 01:07:45.629
Sniff check!

1196
01:07:45.762 --> 01:07:47.531
(YELPING)

1197
01:07:47.631 --> 01:07:49.999
Ooh. that's Avatar material
right there.

1198
01:07:50.100 --> 01:07:52.469
Yes. it is. Oh!

1199
01:07:52.602 --> 01:07:53.670
Yes. yes. yes. yes. yes.

1200
01:07:53.770 --> 01:07:56.173
It appears the universe
has brought us together

1201
01:07:56.273 --> 01:07:58.775
for a very important mission...

1202
01:07:58.908 --> 01:08:00.277
Ah?

1203
01:08:00.410 --> 01:08:01.711
...to flee!

1204
01:08:02.246 --> 01:08:03.747
Run for your lives!

1205
01:08:03.880 --> 01:08:05.249
Wait. come back!

1206
01:08:05.382 --> 01:08:06.916
You're going the wrong way!

1207
01:08:07.050 --> 01:08:08.118
Stop!

1208
01:08:08.785 --> 01:08:10.420
Please. Great Spirit.
both of our worlds
are in danger!

1209
01:08:10.554 --> 01:08:14.258
No. no. no. no. no. no.
I am not going back up there.

1210
01:08:14.391 --> 01:08:15.659
(GASPS)

1211
01:08:17.461 --> 01:08:18.528
(CHITTERS)

1212
01:08:19.363 --> 01:08:22.799
Hmm. Well. when you
put it like that.
it does make more sense.

1213
01:08:23.700 --> 01:08:26.203
Upon reflection.
I've decided I shall help you

1214
01:08:26.303 --> 01:08:27.604
and your human-y friends.

1215
01:08:27.737 --> 01:08:30.106
What did he say?
Nice work. Momo.

1216
01:08:30.240 --> 01:08:32.342
All right. in you go.

1217
01:08:35.179 --> 01:08:36.646
By the way.
no eating anything you find

1218
01:08:36.813 --> 01:08:38.715
in my teeth. as I'm
saving that for later.

1219
01:08:39.216 --> 01:08:41.151
Ready. set. get steady and ret.

1220
01:08:41.285 --> 01:08:44.321
One and a two
and a you know what to do.

1221
01:08:44.488 --> 01:08:45.855
Blast off!

1222
01:08:46.022 --> 01:08:47.991
(ALL SHOUTING)

1223
01:08:50.760 --> 01:08:53.430
I know we haven't known
each other very long. but...

1224
01:08:53.530 --> 01:08:54.898
I love you!

1225
01:08:54.998 --> 01:08:56.600
You don't have to say it back.

1226
01:09:00.036 --> 01:09:01.938
(ALL GRUNT)

1227
01:09:05.342 --> 01:09:06.776
Hey! You got your hair back!

1228
01:09:06.910 --> 01:09:09.879
Why are my eyes teary?
Was I crying?

1229
01:09:10.680 --> 01:09:12.449
No way! Look!

1230
01:09:12.549 --> 01:09:13.983
What?
What is it?

1231
01:09:14.117 --> 01:09:15.885
AANG: It's Republic City.

1232
01:09:16.486 --> 01:09:18.688
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1233
01:09:19.155 --> 01:09:21.958
We can't let him destroy
everything we built!

1234
01:09:22.091 --> 01:09:23.593
We won't.

1235
01:09:24.027 --> 01:09:26.196
(CLAMORING)

1236
01:09:26.363 --> 01:09:28.965
(DRAMATIC MUSIC INTENSIFIES)

1237
01:09:38.875 --> 01:09:40.109
Boomerang!

1238
01:09:40.644 --> 01:09:41.878
(GRUNTS)

1239
01:09:45.882 --> 01:09:47.517
(GRUNTING)

1240
01:09:47.651 --> 01:09:49.319
(GRUNTING)

1241
01:09:57.494 --> 01:09:58.795
Give me the staff. Tagah!

1242
01:09:58.895 --> 01:10:01.398
I see I underestimated you.
Avatar.

1243
01:10:01.565 --> 01:10:04.501
Your friends are stronger
than I thought.

1244
01:10:04.634 --> 01:10:06.270
But you're too late.

1245
01:10:06.770 --> 01:10:08.305
(ALL SHOUTING)

1246
01:10:14.511 --> 01:10:15.645
The Denied.

1247
01:10:16.079 --> 01:10:18.815
You see?
I did what you wanted. Aang.

1248
01:10:18.915 --> 01:10:21.485
I returned airbending
to the world.

1249
01:10:21.585 --> 01:10:22.986
(CHUCKLES)

1250
01:10:23.086 --> 01:10:24.254
What's the plan?

1251
01:10:24.721 --> 01:10:27.524
We'll deal with the Denied.
You have to get the staff.

1252
01:10:27.791 --> 01:10:30.827
I will rebuild Jharana
on the ruins of our enemies.

1253
01:10:30.927 --> 01:10:32.729
just as they did on ours.

1254
01:10:32.862 --> 01:10:35.599
A new Air Empire will rise.

1255
01:10:36.099 --> 01:10:37.601
Kill them all.

1256
01:10:37.734 --> 01:10:39.903
(ALL SHOUTING)

1257
01:10:40.036 --> 01:10:42.038
(ALL GRUNTING)

1258
01:10:48.478 --> 01:10:50.179
(WHIMPERING)

1259
01:10:55.852 --> 01:10:58.054
We have to get
these people out of here.

1260
01:11:02.459 --> 01:11:03.793
(SHOUTS)

1261
01:11:09.132 --> 01:11:11.067
(GROANS. GASPS)

1262
01:11:14.371 --> 01:11:15.939
Oh. yeah!

1263
01:11:22.979 --> 01:11:24.247
AANG: Tagah!

1264
01:11:24.381 --> 01:11:25.749
Give it to me!

1265
01:11:27.484 --> 01:11:28.752
This isn't the way!

1266
01:11:28.885 --> 01:11:31.888
We can use the staff
to bring back balance. peace!

1267
01:11:31.988 --> 01:11:34.057
You care so much
about your ideals

1268
01:11:34.157 --> 01:11:35.992
that you let
your people die!

1269
01:11:36.660 --> 01:11:39.363
I will do anything
to make sure they survive!

1270
01:11:40.029 --> 01:11:41.197
(GRUNTS)

1271
01:11:46.770 --> 01:11:47.771
(GROANS)

1272
01:11:47.871 --> 01:11:49.839
(CLAMORING)

1273
01:11:51.007 --> 01:11:52.742
(GROWLS)

1274
01:11:55.111 --> 01:11:57.313
(SCREECHING)

1275
01:11:57.814 --> 01:11:59.749
My cabbages!
Not my cabbages!

1276
01:11:59.849 --> 01:12:01.117
(SCREAMS)

1277
01:12:05.422 --> 01:12:08.057
(SNIFFLES) My cabbages!

1278
01:12:08.224 --> 01:12:11.928
My cabbages!

1279
01:12:19.669 --> 01:12:21.304
(YELLS)

1280
01:12:21.438 --> 01:12:22.939
(BOTH GRUNT)

1281
01:12:24.207 --> 01:12:25.375
Don't do this.

1282
01:12:25.642 --> 01:12:28.277
You have the power now.
You can decide how to use it.

1283
01:12:28.378 --> 01:12:29.379
I'm not like you.

1284
01:12:29.513 --> 01:12:30.880
The world hasn't
been good to me.

1285
01:12:31.047 --> 01:12:32.749
The world is what we make it.

1286
01:12:33.082 --> 01:12:34.618
JIE: Get away from her!

1287
01:12:38.354 --> 01:12:39.589
(GRUNTS)

1288
01:12:41.558 --> 01:12:42.992
(YELLS)

1289
01:12:51.735 --> 01:12:53.837
(CLAMORING CONTINUES)

1290
01:13:06.783 --> 01:13:08.184
Tagah. stop!

1291
01:13:11.387 --> 01:13:13.056
(SHOUTS)

1292
01:13:13.189 --> 01:13:15.224
You betrayed me!
You betrayed our culture!

1293
01:13:15.358 --> 01:13:17.894
I gave you every chance
to see the truth!

1294
01:13:23.833 --> 01:13:26.202
Shouldn't you be
in the Fire Nation?

1295
01:13:28.071 --> 01:13:30.574
I'm fighting for the peace
of all nations!

1296
01:13:33.877 --> 01:13:36.012
Big talk from someone
who sits on a throne

1297
01:13:36.112 --> 01:13:37.847
built on a century of war!

1298
01:13:43.052 --> 01:13:45.021
(ROCKS RUMBLING)

1299
01:13:46.756 --> 01:13:50.059
(METAL CREAKING)

1300
01:13:51.828 --> 01:13:56.966
(ALL GRUNTING)

1301
01:14:00.804 --> 01:14:04.407
I'm still the greatest
Earthbender in the world!

1302
01:14:08.011 --> 01:14:09.479
(BLADE DINGS)

1303
01:14:14.350 --> 01:14:18.655
(AIR WHISTLES)

1304
01:14:23.860 --> 01:14:25.328
(BOTH GRUNT)

1305
01:14:28.164 --> 01:14:31.000
Oh. no.
I'm out of water.

1306
01:14:32.502 --> 01:14:34.571
(CACKLES) We got ya!

1307
01:14:34.971 --> 01:14:37.541
And there's no Avatar
here to save you.

1308
01:14:39.142 --> 01:14:41.444
SOKKA: Sokka-Cycle!
Huh?

1309
01:14:42.311 --> 01:14:43.813
(BELL DINGING)
(HOPEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

1310
01:14:43.947 --> 01:14:44.914
(GASPS)

1311
01:14:45.014 --> 01:14:46.816
Let's see if
your fancy new bending

1312
01:14:46.950 --> 01:14:49.619
can beat some good old
nonbending know-how.

1313
01:14:53.690 --> 01:14:56.225
(GROANING)

1314
01:14:56.726 --> 01:14:58.461
SOKKA: Bombs away!

1315
01:15:00.129 --> 01:15:01.731
(DENIED MEMBERS GRUNTING)

1316
01:15:04.668 --> 01:15:06.603
You just got denied!

1317
01:15:07.804 --> 01:15:09.038
Whoa!

1318
01:15:09.372 --> 01:15:12.041
(DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES)

1319
01:15:14.410 --> 01:15:15.478
(ALL COUGHING)

1320
01:15:15.812 --> 01:15:18.414
Let's go!
Good luck saving your city.

1321
01:15:19.348 --> 01:15:20.416
Huh?
(GASPS)

1322
01:15:23.553 --> 01:15:25.722
(CITIZENS SCREAMING)

1323
01:15:26.189 --> 01:15:28.958
We have to save
as many people as we can.

1324
01:15:29.392 --> 01:15:33.730
(CITIZEN YELPS. PANTS)

1325
01:15:39.235 --> 01:15:41.470
(BOTH GRUNT)

1326
01:15:44.874 --> 01:15:45.942
(GASPS)

1327
01:15:47.276 --> 01:15:48.678
AANG: I know your pain.

1328
01:15:48.812 --> 01:15:50.747
I know what you've been through.

1329
01:15:51.547 --> 01:15:52.849
You don't know.

1330
01:15:53.583 --> 01:15:57.687
I watched as all of my brothers
and sisters were slaughtered.

1331
01:15:58.321 --> 01:16:02.125
When the Fire Nation
burned the Air Nomads to ash.

1332
01:16:02.291 --> 01:16:03.426
where were you?

1333
01:16:04.427 --> 01:16:05.595
You ran!

1334
01:16:05.762 --> 01:16:07.330
(MUSIC INTENSIFIES)

1335
01:16:26.382 --> 01:16:27.651
Tagah!

1336
01:16:37.761 --> 01:16:38.662
No!

1337
01:16:42.766 --> 01:16:44.467
(MUSIC ENDS ABRUPTLY)

1338
01:16:44.768 --> 01:16:48.371
(WHOOSHES)

1339
01:16:51.107 --> 01:16:54.678
(CITIZENS CLAMORING)

1340
01:17:01.217 --> 01:17:06.489
The full power
of the Spirit World
flows through me!

1341
01:17:06.622 --> 01:17:09.425
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

1342
01:17:16.165 --> 01:17:18.735
This is what strength
looks like!

1343
01:17:29.846 --> 01:17:30.747
(SHOUTS)

1344
01:17:35.719 --> 01:17:38.454
(BOTH GRUNT)

1345
01:17:46.162 --> 01:17:47.430
(GASPS)

1346
01:17:54.738 --> 01:17:56.906
(SHUDDERED BREATHING)

1347
01:18:06.415 --> 01:18:07.616
(CLAMORING)

1348
01:18:07.717 --> 01:18:09.552
(ALL SCREAMING)

1349
01:18:12.188 --> 01:18:14.057
You should've run away
like you did

1350
01:18:14.223 --> 01:18:17.426
all those years ago.
little Avatar.

1351
01:18:18.094 --> 01:18:19.262
I...

1352
01:18:20.329 --> 01:18:21.697
won't run.

1353
01:18:21.931 --> 01:18:26.502
Then at least you'll die
knowing you're not
the last Airbender!

1354
01:18:31.908 --> 01:18:33.109
(GASPS)

1355
01:18:50.359 --> 01:18:52.595
(SHOUTS)

1356
01:19:03.306 --> 01:19:04.673
TAGAH: Aang!

1357
01:19:12.515 --> 01:19:13.382
No!

1358
01:19:13.482 --> 01:19:14.818
(SHOUTS)

1359
01:19:20.589 --> 01:19:22.826
(CLAMORING)
(ROARS)

1360
01:19:22.959 --> 01:19:24.060
(CHITTERS)

1361
01:19:39.442 --> 01:19:41.010
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1362
01:19:44.380 --> 01:19:45.514
No.

1363
01:19:54.690 --> 01:19:56.592
(CHIMING)

1364
01:19:56.759 --> 01:19:58.761
(CLATTERING)

1365
01:20:04.700 --> 01:20:06.069
(SHOUTS)

1366
01:20:16.679 --> 01:20:17.813
(GRUNTS)

1367
01:20:20.549 --> 01:20:22.818
We could've been brothers!

1368
01:20:23.286 --> 01:20:25.154
We could've done this together!

1369
01:20:25.288 --> 01:20:27.790
It didn't have to end like this!

1370
01:20:33.062 --> 01:20:34.397
It's Aang!
He's got the staff!

1371
01:20:34.530 --> 01:20:36.933
Yeah!
Kick his butt. Mega Aang!

1372
01:20:37.066 --> 01:20:38.567
No! Something's wrong!

1373
01:20:38.701 --> 01:20:40.803
The power is corrupting him!

1374
01:20:48.244 --> 01:20:50.613
(SCREAMS)

1375
01:20:51.847 --> 01:20:54.083
(GROANS)

1376
01:20:56.252 --> 01:20:58.421
(GROANING)

1377
01:20:58.587 --> 01:21:00.990
AANG: I dreamt of bringing
the Air Nomads back

1378
01:21:01.090 --> 01:21:02.758
to the world
as peacekeepers.

1379
01:21:02.892 --> 01:21:04.693
They could have been
a beacon of light

1380
01:21:04.827 --> 01:21:06.095
for the world to follow.

1381
01:21:06.262 --> 01:21:07.630
But you ruined it!

1382
01:21:07.796 --> 01:21:10.166
You twisted my dream
into a nightmare!

1383
01:21:10.699 --> 01:21:14.537
Finally. you have the power
the Air Nomads need.

1384
01:21:14.670 --> 01:21:17.106
Maybe there is hope
for you after all.

1385
01:21:17.240 --> 01:21:18.407
(GRUMBLES)

1386
01:21:19.508 --> 01:21:22.011
(SHOUTING)

1387
01:21:22.445 --> 01:21:24.347
(SCREAMS)

1388
01:21:27.583 --> 01:21:30.453
Do it!
Use the staff!

1389
01:21:30.586 --> 01:21:33.556
Show me you have the strength
to bring our people back!

1390
01:21:34.557 --> 01:21:35.658
Do it!

1391
01:21:35.791 --> 01:21:37.994
(SHOUTING)

1392
01:21:43.566 --> 01:21:45.168
(DRAMATIC MUSIC STOPS ABRUPTLY)

1393
01:21:45.301 --> 01:21:47.370
(PEACEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

1394
01:21:59.048 --> 01:22:00.883
(CHILDREN GIGGLING)

1395
01:22:05.854 --> 01:22:07.590
(LAUGHS)

1396
01:22:12.461 --> 01:22:13.829
GYATSO: <i>Aang.</i>

1397
01:22:16.165 --> 01:22:19.435
<i>You will do so many great things
as the Avatar.</i>

1398
01:22:19.969 --> 01:22:23.906
<i>but you must be prepared
to do what frightens you
the most.</i>

1399
01:22:25.441 --> 01:22:30.413
<i>Your people. your home.
we are always with you.</i>

1400
01:22:36.385 --> 01:22:39.055
(GROANING)
(DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES)

1401
01:22:46.895 --> 01:22:48.031
No.

1402
01:22:54.137 --> 01:22:55.538
No!

1403
01:23:02.711 --> 01:23:05.614
(GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING)

1404
01:23:14.890 --> 01:23:15.924
(SHOUTS)

1405
01:23:16.059 --> 01:23:17.460
(BOTH WHIMPER)

1406
01:23:17.560 --> 01:23:18.594
(GASPS)

1407
01:23:18.761 --> 01:23:21.130
No! My power!

1408
01:23:27.270 --> 01:23:28.571
No.

1409
01:23:29.072 --> 01:23:30.273
No!

1410
01:23:34.610 --> 01:23:36.479
(GROANS. PANTS)

1411
01:23:39.748 --> 01:23:40.883
You fool!

1412
01:23:41.016 --> 01:23:42.451
Why?

1413
01:23:42.951 --> 01:23:44.820
Why did you break it?

1414
01:23:45.254 --> 01:23:48.857
We could have fixed everything.

1415
01:23:48.991 --> 01:23:51.727
We can't erase
the pain of the past.

1416
01:23:52.895 --> 01:23:54.130
We couldn't save them.

1417
01:23:54.297 --> 01:23:57.966
But it's our duty
to protect our people.

1418
01:23:58.134 --> 01:24:01.370
Not at the cost of betraying
everything they stood for.

1419
01:24:01.470 --> 01:24:02.771
No.

1420
01:24:03.272 --> 01:24:04.973
It's time to let go.

1421
01:24:05.941 --> 01:24:07.876
You have to forgive yourself.

1422
01:24:10.446 --> 01:24:12.715
I have to forgive myself too.

1423
01:24:21.557 --> 01:24:24.593
Air nomads are formed
from the mist.

1424
01:24:28.464 --> 01:24:32.501
BOTH: We walk the world
for a moment in time.

1425
01:24:34.803 --> 01:24:39.142
Then we return
to the eternal wind.

1426
01:24:52.488 --> 01:24:54.223
(GROWLS)

1427
01:24:55.191 --> 01:24:56.759
(GASPS) Aang!

1428
01:25:00.296 --> 01:25:02.030
Hey. Katara.

1429
01:25:02.165 --> 01:25:03.332
Hey. Aang.

1430
01:25:05.834 --> 01:25:06.835
Seriously?

1431
01:25:06.969 --> 01:25:09.138
You do realize
you're falling. right?

1432
01:25:09.272 --> 01:25:11.574
Hey. if you ever get tired
of relying on Appa.

1433
01:25:11.674 --> 01:25:13.876
I could hook you up
with one of these babies.

1434
01:25:14.009 --> 01:25:15.278
(WHIMPERING)

1435
01:25:15.411 --> 01:25:17.012
(BOTH LAUGHING)

1436
01:25:18.847 --> 01:25:21.184
SOKKA: I'll give you
the best friend discount!

1437
01:25:29.792 --> 01:25:31.827
(CHATTERING)

1438
01:25:31.960 --> 01:25:33.296
These are pretty good!

1439
01:25:35.231 --> 01:25:37.700
AANG: <i>I don't know
if airbending will ever return.</i>

1440
01:25:38.267 --> 01:25:40.068
<i>but I know now
that the true power</i>

1441
01:25:40.203 --> 01:25:43.239
of the Air Nomads
was never their bending.

1442
01:25:43.806 --> 01:25:45.174
It was their values.

1443
01:25:45.874 --> 01:25:49.312
And that's a power
I can pass on to others.

1444
01:25:49.412 --> 01:25:52.781
Avatar Aang. you are
the true embodiment

1445
01:25:52.881 --> 01:25:54.417
of the Air Nomads.

1446
01:25:55.251 --> 01:25:58.487
Thank you for giving up
the power that I could not.

1447
01:25:59.154 --> 01:26:02.391
You give me hope for the future
of our culture.

1448
01:26:03.058 --> 01:26:06.229
(EPIC ETHEREAL MUSIC PLAYING)

1449
01:26:16.339 --> 01:26:18.073
It's amazing. isn't it?

1450
01:26:18.707 --> 01:26:21.744
The first new air temple
in centuries.

1451
01:26:22.745 --> 01:26:25.448
Republic City
is finally complete.

1452
01:26:29.285 --> 01:26:32.888
A city for all nations.
just like you promised.

1453
01:26:33.789 --> 01:26:36.292
I never could have done this
without you. Katara.

1454
01:26:37.760 --> 01:26:38.961
Hey. everybody.

1455
01:26:39.094 --> 01:26:40.763
Sorry I kept you all waiting.

1456
01:26:40.929 --> 01:26:42.765
Are you ready for our big trip?

1457
01:26:43.866 --> 01:26:47.370
As my new acolytes. you'll be
helping me preserve our culture

1458
01:26:47.470 --> 01:26:48.971
for future generations.

1459
01:26:49.738 --> 01:26:52.408
So. who wants
to search for artifacts

1460
01:26:52.541 --> 01:26:54.142
at an ancient
abandoned temple?

1461
01:26:54.310 --> 01:26:55.378
(FLATLY) Yay.

1462
01:26:55.644 --> 01:26:56.812
I'm only going
to make sure you don't try

1463
01:26:56.979 --> 01:26:59.382
to release another
beefy old Airbender.

1464
01:26:59.515 --> 01:27:01.817
Yeah. I'm done
with bad boys.

1465
01:27:13.762 --> 01:27:15.864
AANG: Avatar Sonam told me
about this place.

1466
01:27:15.964 --> 01:27:18.567
So it's very possible
that no one's been here

1467
01:27:18.667 --> 01:27:20.336
in hundreds of years.

1468
01:27:21.570 --> 01:27:24.373
Oh! Is this
an Airbender relic?

1469
01:27:24.473 --> 01:27:26.108
I think that's just a rock.

1470
01:27:26.241 --> 01:27:27.976
But I love the enthusiasm.

1471
01:27:28.777 --> 01:27:30.479
(CHIRPS)
Aw!

1472
01:27:30.613 --> 01:27:32.214
(ROARS)
(YELPS)

1473
01:27:34.016 --> 01:27:35.183
AANG: Keep your eyes open.

1474
01:27:35.318 --> 01:27:37.353
You never know what
we might discover here.

1475
01:27:39.021 --> 01:27:40.323
Woah!

1476
01:27:46.929 --> 01:27:48.497
I thought they were extinct.

1477
01:27:48.664 --> 01:27:50.032
(ROARS)

1478
01:27:55.838 --> 01:27:57.373
I can't believe it.

1479
01:27:58.040 --> 01:27:59.975
The original Airbenders.

1480
01:28:07.115 --> 01:28:09.352
Aw. can I have one?

1481
01:28:09.485 --> 01:28:10.553
(LAUGHS)

1482
01:28:10.719 --> 01:28:12.755
Appa. yip yip!

1483
01:28:24.967 --> 01:28:27.503
(PEACEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

1483
01:28:28.305 --> 01:29:28.383
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
